1
00:00:05,207 --> 00:00:07,642
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:10,878
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:10,912 --> 00:00:13,882
♪ THERE WAS A GUY NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:16,350
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:20,088
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:20,122 --> 00:00:23,057
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:26,093
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:26,127 --> 00:00:30,732
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM
SO THEY SHOT HIM INTO SPACE ♪

9
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:35,903
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

10
00:00:35,937 --> 00:00:38,940
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

11
00:00:38,973 --> 00:00:41,877
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

12
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:45,113
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:45,147 --> 00:00:48,215
♪ NOW, KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

14
00:00:48,248 --> 00:00:51,352
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:54,488
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

16
00:00:54,522 --> 00:00:57,992
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

17
00:00:59,227 --> 00:01:01,095
LET'S GO.

18
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:02,397
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

19
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:03,732
HI, GIRL.

20
00:01:03,765 --> 00:01:05,500
WHAT A COOL GUY.

21
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:07,068
A WISECRACKER.

22
00:01:07,102 --> 00:01:10,205
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

23
00:01:10,238 --> 00:01:13,442
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

24
00:01:13,475 --> 00:01:16,410
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

25
00:01:16,443 --> 00:01:19,280
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

26
00:01:19,313 --> 00:01:22,350
♪ FOR MYSTERY
SCIENCE THEATER ♪

27
00:01:22,383 --> 00:01:24,418
♪ 3000 ♪

28
00:01:34,795 --> 00:01:37,832
ALL RIGHT, F-STOP AT 5.6.

29
00:01:37,865 --> 00:01:40,502
FOR MAXIMUM DEPTH OF FIELD.

30
00:01:40,535 --> 00:01:41,735
OKAY, THAT LOOKS GOOD.

31
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,672
OKAY, 5.6

32
00:01:43,705 --> 00:01:46,307
AT, LET'S SEE HERE, EIGHT FEET.

33
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:50,245
THAT COMES
TO ROUGHLY A.S.A. OF 200.

34
00:01:50,278 --> 00:01:52,980
OKAY, ADJUST LIGHTING
TO FULL LUMENS

35
00:01:53,013 --> 00:01:54,648
AND A CONE FOCUS.

36
00:01:54,682 --> 00:01:57,552
THAT LOOKS GOOD.
OKAY, BRING AROUND
THE BACK DROPS.

37
00:01:57,585 --> 00:01:59,153
STAY CHEERY, EVERYBODY.

38
00:01:59,187 --> 00:02:00,722
OKAY.

39
00:02:00,755 --> 00:02:02,923
OH, HI, EVERYBODY.
WELCOME TO THE SATELLITE
OF LOVE.

40
00:02:02,957 --> 00:02:04,092
I'M JOEL ROBINSON,

41
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,393
AND I JUST THOUGHT
IT WOULD BE NICE

42
00:02:05,427 --> 00:02:06,862
TO GET A NICE PICTURE
OF THE BOYS

43
00:02:06,895 --> 00:02:07,995
TO HAVE AROUND THE HOUSE,

44
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:09,597
SO I'M TAKING THEIR PORTRAIT,

45
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,498
AND I'LL BE WITH YOU
IN A MINUTE.

46
00:02:11,532 --> 00:02:13,300
COULD WE JUST GO, PLEASE?

47
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,035
- ORDER. ORDER.
- STOP IT, YOU TWO.

48
00:02:15,068 --> 00:02:16,637
THEY WERE LIKE THIS
ALL THE WAY OVER.

49
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:18,807
- YOU GUYS, LISTEN--
- CUT IT OUT, FEMBOT.

50
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,008
WE ARE GOING TO GET
A NICE PICTURE

51
00:02:21,042 --> 00:02:22,210
OF THIS FAMILY

52
00:02:22,243 --> 00:02:24,178
IF IT KILLS US.
- [BLOWS RASPBERRIES]

53
00:02:24,212 --> 00:02:26,047
- CROW.
- HEY, WHAT?

54
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:30,285
- CROW, WHERE ARE THOSE NICE
PANTS I BOUGHT YOU?
- I DON'T KNOW.

55
00:02:30,318 --> 00:02:32,087
YOU CAN'T WALK AROUND
WEARING A SPORT COAT

56
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,622
WITHOUT YOUR NICE PANTS.

57
00:02:33,655 --> 00:02:35,122
CAN WE JUST GO?

58
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:37,758
COMMERCIAL SIGN IN 10 SECONDS.
SAY CHEESE.

59
00:02:37,792 --> 00:02:41,395
OKAY. NOW, COME ON, YOU GUYS.
SHAPE UP, FACE CAMBOT.

60
00:02:41,428 --> 00:02:42,797
COME ON, GYPSY.
GET IN HERE.

61
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:44,198
OH, MY HAIR.

62
00:02:44,232 --> 00:02:45,400
HOLD IT.

63
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:46,700
HEY. THE LIGHT METER, JOEL.

64
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:48,002
- OH.
- [SHUTTER CLICKS]

65
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:51,005
[ALL GROAN]

66
00:02:57,145 --> 00:02:58,212
JOEL. JOEL.

67
00:02:58,245 --> 00:02:59,547
OOH, SNICKER SNACKS.

68
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,582
JOEL.

69
00:03:00,615 --> 00:03:02,183
CHOCOLATE MILK...

70
00:03:02,217 --> 00:03:05,085
YOU GUYS, WOULD YOU PLEASE GET
BACK INTO POSITION?

71
00:03:05,118 --> 00:03:07,622
COME ON, KNOCK IT OFF.

72
00:03:07,655 --> 00:03:09,790
- JOEL, I JUST--
- GYPSY, COME ON.

73
00:03:09,823 --> 00:03:11,927
- SPEED AND CHIM-CHIM
ARE CALLING.
- STOP IT.

74
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,928
OKAY, THANKS A LOT.
SORRY ABOUT THE TIP.

75
00:03:13,962 --> 00:03:16,863
I LEFT THE MONEY IN MY OTHER,
UH, POCKET.

76
00:03:16,898 --> 00:03:18,365
OH! HI, JOEL.

77
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:19,967
HOW YOU DOING?
WE'LL BE WITH YOU
IN ONE SECOND.

78
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,970
CLAYTON. HERE, BOY.

79
00:03:22,003 --> 00:03:24,572
COME HERE, CLAYTON.
HERE, BOY.
HERE, CLAYTON.

80
00:03:24,605 --> 00:03:27,208
GIVE ME ONE GOOD REASON
WHY I SHOULDN'T KILL YOU,
FRANK.

81
00:03:27,242 --> 00:03:28,577
WELL, THE STUFF IS HERE.

82
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:30,077
THE STUFF THAT WE ORDERED--

83
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:31,878
JUST IN TIME
FOR THE INVENTION EXCHANGE.

84
00:03:31,913 --> 00:03:35,483
YOU GO FIRST, PUMPKIN PANTS.

85
00:03:35,517 --> 00:03:37,352
WELL, YOUR AMPLE ONES.

86
00:03:37,385 --> 00:03:38,953
MY INVENTION EXCHANGE
THIS WEEK

87
00:03:38,987 --> 00:03:41,722
DYNAMICALLY BLENDS MARTIAL ARTS
WITH SNACKING.

88
00:03:41,755 --> 00:03:42,923
IT'S CALLED SNACTION,

89
00:03:42,957 --> 00:03:44,958
AND IT MAKES SNACKING FUN.

90
00:03:44,992 --> 00:03:46,593
HERE'S A SNACTION FAVORITE--

91
00:03:46,627 --> 00:03:48,663
THE WAX KNUCKLES.
ALL RIGHT?

92
00:03:48,697 --> 00:03:49,730
AND HERE'S ONE.

93
00:03:49,763 --> 00:03:51,232
IT'S CALLED A PIXIE STAFF.

94
00:03:51,265 --> 00:03:53,100
[GRUNTS]

95
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,202
IT'S A PIXIE STICK

96
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:58,138
FILLED WITH DELICIOUS
STRAIGHT SUGAR.

97
00:03:58,172 --> 00:03:59,373
SEE? OKAY?

98
00:03:59,407 --> 00:04:01,642
AND, HEY, CROW.
HEY, CROW.

99
00:04:01,675 --> 00:04:03,678
WHAT ARE THESE HERE?
WHAT ARE THESE?

100
00:04:03,712 --> 00:04:05,813
- WHAT ARE WHICH ONES?
- WHAT ARE THESE?

101
00:04:05,847 --> 00:04:09,983
OH, THEM ARE THE FIVE LADY
FINGERS OF DEATH.

102
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:12,287
FIVE LADY FINGERS OF DEATH.
YOU GET IT?

103
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,655
AND THIS IS BASED
ON A CHUCK NORRIS MOVIE.

104
00:04:14,688 --> 00:04:17,692
IT'S CALLED THE EVERLASTING
OCTA--GOBSTOPPER.

105
00:04:17,725 --> 00:04:18,793
YOU GET IT?

106
00:04:18,827 --> 00:04:21,895
OH, AND THESE ARE NINJA
THROWING COOKIES.

107
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:23,530
HEY, THOSE ARE DELICIOUS.

108
00:04:23,563 --> 00:04:25,967
YOU SEE, EVERYBODY
DOESN'T LIKE SOME THINGS,

109
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,402
BUT NOBODY
DOESN'T LIKE BRUCE LEE.

110
00:04:27,435 --> 00:04:28,770
OUCH.

111
00:04:28,803 --> 00:04:31,305
UH-OH, I BROKE HIM.

112
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:33,273
OH, WELL, THAT'S REALLY GREAT,
JOEL,

113
00:04:33,307 --> 00:04:34,875
BUT WE'VE GOT SOMETHING
GOING DOWN HERE

114
00:04:34,908 --> 00:04:36,910
- THAT'S REALLY SPECIAL.
- TELL THEM, FRANK.

115
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,747
WELL, DR. FORRESTER
HAS TAKEN THE MONEY

116
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:40,147
FROM MY 401 K

117
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:42,783
AND SUNK IT INTO THESE
FAST-FOOD NOVELTY ITEMS,

118
00:04:42,817 --> 00:04:46,253
WHICH HE'S JUST SOLD
TO A MAJOR, MAJOR BUYER

119
00:04:46,287 --> 00:04:48,255
WHO SHALL REMAIN NAMELESS.

120
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,857
WELL, ACTUALLY
THAT FELL THROUGH,

121
00:04:49,890 --> 00:04:51,525
BUT I'M SURE
THEY'RE GOING TO SELL.

122
00:04:51,558 --> 00:04:53,695
YOU SEE, JOEL,
THEY'RE CALLED UNHAPPY MEALS.

123
00:04:53,728 --> 00:04:56,197
YOU TOOK MY MONEY AND YOU
HAVEN'T SOLD THEM YET?

124
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:58,498
OH, QUIT WHINING, FRANK.

125
00:04:58,532 --> 00:04:59,933
AS AN EXAMPLE, JOEL.

126
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:02,603
THIS ONE COMES
FROM THE RESTAURANT

127
00:05:02,637 --> 00:05:04,305
WITH A COLD
HAMBURGER SANDWICH

128
00:05:04,338 --> 00:05:07,242
WITH A BITE TAKEN OUT OF IT,

129
00:05:07,275 --> 00:05:09,543
SOME FLOOR SWEEPING COMPOUND,

130
00:05:09,577 --> 00:05:11,212
A COUPLE OF DEAD SILVERFISH,

131
00:05:11,245 --> 00:05:13,247
AND A RUSTY SUTURE NEEDLE.

132
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,282
YOU TOOK ALL MY MONEY,
YOU SON OF A...

133
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:16,850
WATCH IT, FRANK.

134
00:05:16,883 --> 00:05:18,920
NOW, THERE ARE MANY
DIFFERENT STYLES, JOEL.

135
00:05:18,953 --> 00:05:21,722
FOR INSTANCE,
THIS ONE COMES WITH A MAZE,

136
00:05:21,755 --> 00:05:23,357
AND YOU TRY TO GET
THE MOTORCADE

137
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,225
PAST THE BOOK DEPOSITORY.

138
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:26,560
[CHUCKLES]

139
00:05:26,593 --> 00:05:28,062
AND THEN THIS ONE COMES

140
00:05:28,095 --> 00:05:30,330
WITH A USED Q-TIP.

141
00:05:30,365 --> 00:05:31,832
OOH, THAT IS UNHAPPY.
ISN'T IT?

142
00:05:31,865 --> 00:05:33,902
AND THEN THERE'S ONE
WITH A ROACH MOTEL,

143
00:05:33,935 --> 00:05:35,470
AND, WELL, YOU GET THE IDEA.

144
00:05:35,503 --> 00:05:37,905
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

145
00:05:37,938 --> 00:05:40,307
I THINK IT'S EVIL
AND IT'LL NEVER SELL.

146
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,708
YEAH, AND GIVE FRANK
HIS MONEY BACK.

147
00:05:41,742 --> 00:05:42,910
YEAH.

148
00:05:42,943 --> 00:05:44,512
OH, BLOW IT OUT YOUR--

149
00:05:44,545 --> 00:05:46,513
EXPERIMENT TODAY

150
00:05:46,547 --> 00:05:48,348
IS A SWEDISH FANTASY CALLED

151
00:05:48,382 --> 00:05:50,117
THE DAY THE EARTH FROZE,

152
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:52,187
BUT FIRST A SHORT,

153
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,253
APPLY TITLED

154
00:05:53,287 --> 00:05:54,288
"HERE COMES THE CIRCUS,"

155
00:05:54,322 --> 00:05:55,890
AND I HOPE IT GOES DOWN HARD.

156
00:05:55,923 --> 00:05:58,025
- PUSH THE BUTTON, FRANK.
- NO, I WANT MY MONEY BACK.

157
00:05:58,058 --> 00:05:59,327
FORCEPS, FRANK.
PAIN.

158
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,762
I DON'T CARE.
I WANT MY MONEY.

159
00:06:00,795 --> 00:06:03,397
- ELECTROSHOCK FOR A--
PUSH THE BUTTON.
- NO! NO!

160
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:04,565
THE BOX, FRANK.

161
00:06:04,598 --> 00:06:05,767
PUSH THE BUTTON.

162
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,867
YES...
[MUTTERS]

163
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,903
- [ALARM BLARING]
- [ALL YELLING]

164
00:06:19,513 --> 00:06:21,282
OW. OWY.

165
00:06:21,315 --> 00:06:24,152
THINK YOU BROKE MY BONE.

166
00:06:24,185 --> 00:06:26,653
HERE COMES THE DEVIL!
[CACKLES]

167
00:06:26,687 --> 00:06:28,155
BEELZEBUB THE CLOWN.

168
00:06:28,188 --> 00:06:30,858
GUYS, CAN WE BE JUST A LITTLE
LESS DARK WITH THIS SHORT?

169
00:06:30,892 --> 00:06:33,560
DARK?

170
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:34,895
DARK.

171
00:06:34,928 --> 00:06:36,330
THERE'S EXCITEMENT EVERYWHERE.

172
00:06:36,363 --> 00:06:37,598
THE CIRCUS IS HERE.

173
00:06:37,632 --> 00:06:39,167
EVERYONE IS HEADED
FOR THE BIG TOP

174
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,333
TO THRILL TO AND CHEER

175
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:42,170
THE FUNMAKERS, DAREDEVILS,

176
00:06:42,203 --> 00:06:44,338
FREAKS AND FEROCIOUS
PERFORMING ANIMALS.

177
00:06:44,372 --> 00:06:45,940
AND HERE COME THE FREAKS NOW.

178
00:06:45,973 --> 00:06:47,942
LOOK AT THEM ALL.

179
00:06:47,975 --> 00:06:49,510
IT'S A DIME FOR SOME CANDY

180
00:06:49,543 --> 00:06:52,078
AND MAYBE A TUMMY ACHE
TOMORROW.

181
00:06:52,113 --> 00:06:53,480
CHUG IT! CHUG IT CHUG IT!

182
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:54,915
CANNONBALL! CANNONBALL!

183
00:06:54,948 --> 00:06:56,083
[BELCHES]

184
00:06:56,117 --> 00:06:57,218
PEANUTS FOR THE ELEPHANTS.

185
00:06:57,252 --> 00:06:59,020
NOW, FOLKS,
STEP RIGHT THIS WAY

186
00:06:59,053 --> 00:07:01,855
TO THE BIGGER, BETTER,
MORE EXCITING SIDE SHOW.

187
00:07:01,888 --> 00:07:03,690
NOW, HERE'S THE DEAL.
JUST FOUR YEARS.

188
00:07:03,723 --> 00:07:05,325
CHRISTMAS PRESENT COMING.

189
00:07:05,358 --> 00:07:06,860
...TIME TO SEE IT ALL.

190
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:09,330
GET YOUR RED HOT MOMS.

191
00:07:09,363 --> 00:07:11,798
...LOVELY LITTLE LADY
ON MY RIGHT.

192
00:07:11,832 --> 00:07:14,468
SHE PERFORMS
HER OWN TRACHEOTOMY.

193
00:07:14,502 --> 00:07:18,172
OOH.
[CHUCKLES]

194
00:07:18,205 --> 00:07:19,940
AND SHE'S CUTE, TOO.

195
00:07:19,973 --> 00:07:21,508
EW. UGH.

196
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:23,978
THE SNAKE CHARMER
EXTRAORDINARY.

197
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:27,782
- NOW FOR THE BIG SHOW.
- THE HELL?

198
00:07:27,815 --> 00:07:29,050
THE EVENT THAT THE KIDS
AND THE GROWNUPS

199
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:30,752
HAVE BEEN WAITING
FOR FOR MONTHS.

200
00:07:30,785 --> 00:07:32,887
NO ONE'S GOING TO TELL
A NAVY MAN WHEN HE'S HAD
ENOUGH TO DRINK.

201
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,322
- [BELCHES]
- ...PROUDLY PRESENTS

202
00:07:34,355 --> 00:07:37,325
THE MAGNIFICENT AND GORGEOUS
INAUGURAL PAGEANT.

203
00:07:37,358 --> 00:07:40,562
LOOK, IT'S THOMAS EDISON
WITH HIS ELECTRIC CHILD.

204
00:07:43,663 --> 00:07:47,802
SUPPORTERS DRUMMED UP FOR
THE SPANISH-AMERICAN WAR.

205
00:07:47,835 --> 00:07:52,138
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.
AREN'T THE HORSES SUPPOSED
TO GO BEHIND THE BAND?

206
00:07:52,173 --> 00:07:54,342
WHOOPS.

207
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:58,412
NOW MAKE WAY
FOR THE KU KLUX CLOWNS.
WHOO!

208
00:07:58,445 --> 00:07:59,913
YES, CHILDREN OF ALL AGES

209
00:07:59,947 --> 00:08:01,148
ARE CONFRONTED BY FORCES

210
00:08:01,182 --> 00:08:03,283
THEY CAN'T BEGIN
TO UNDERSTAND.

211
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:05,285
CIGARS? HI, EVERYBODY.

212
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,520
OKAY, GUYS, YOU'RE TOO DARK.

213
00:08:06,553 --> 00:08:07,722
WOULD YOU LIGHTEN UP?

214
00:08:07,755 --> 00:08:09,257
HEY, LOOK.
IT'S RUE MCCLANAHAN.

215
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:14,395
IT'S EZEKIEL,
THAT AMISH CLOWN.

216
00:08:14,428 --> 00:08:17,232
NO BUTTONS.

217
00:08:17,265 --> 00:08:22,203
LOOK, IT'S ICE PRINCESS ZEBRA.

218
00:08:22,237 --> 00:08:23,637
HEY, IT'S EMMETT KELLY.

219
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:26,107
- THAT'S GOOD.
- NO, IT REALLY IS.

220
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:28,408
WHATEVER, JOEL.

221
00:08:31,512 --> 00:08:34,282
AAH! JEEZ.

222
00:08:34,315 --> 00:08:35,850
AAH!

223
00:08:35,883 --> 00:08:37,985
IT'S LIZA!

224
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,787
- AAH!
- NO!

225
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:43,190
...HEADED BY THE WORLD FAMOUS
CLOWN EMMETT KELLY.

226
00:08:43,223 --> 00:08:46,427
SEE? EMMETT CHANGED MANAGEMENT
SOON AFTER THIS.

227
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,762
OH, WE LOVE IT WHEN HE EATS.

228
00:08:48,795 --> 00:08:49,963
INTRODUCING MISS BETTY RICH,

229
00:08:49,997 --> 00:08:51,032
QUEEN OF THE AIR

230
00:08:51,065 --> 00:08:52,267
IN A SENSATIONAL DISPLAY

231
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,935
OF BREATHTAKING AERIAL FEATS

232
00:08:53,968 --> 00:08:55,837
WITHOUT A NET BELOW.

233
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:57,672
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN AMERICA,

234
00:08:57,705 --> 00:08:58,705
MISS BETTY RICH.

235
00:08:58,738 --> 00:09:00,708
WOULD SOMEONE GIVE ME
A HAND HERE?

236
00:09:04,578 --> 00:09:05,947
OOH, BETTY GOT BACK.

237
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:10,050
I'LL SAY.

238
00:09:10,083 --> 00:09:13,220
IT'S A LIVING!

239
00:09:14,688 --> 00:09:16,957
MOTHER, PLEASE COME HOME.

240
00:09:20,193 --> 00:09:22,530
YES, OUR BETTY SWINGS
BOTH WAYS.

241
00:09:22,563 --> 00:09:23,830
OH, STOP IT.

242
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:25,032
SHE DOES.
LOOK.

243
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:26,333
LISTEN, YOU HIT THE FLOOR
A COUPLE OF TIMES,

244
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:27,768
YOU MAKE SURE
YOU GET IT RIGHT.

245
00:09:27,802 --> 00:09:29,103
YEAH, SEE?

246
00:09:39,547 --> 00:09:42,082
THIS TAKES CARE OF UNWANTED
HAIR IN THE BIKINI AREA.

247
00:09:42,115 --> 00:09:44,352
OH! OH! OH! OH!

248
00:09:44,385 --> 00:09:47,422
OH! OH! OH! OH! OH!

249
00:09:47,455 --> 00:09:50,423
THEY TAKE A LICKING
AND KEEP ON TICKING.

250
00:09:51,792 --> 00:09:55,830
WOMEN WHO LOVE TOO MUCH
AND THE FEAT THAT USE THEM.

251
00:09:55,863 --> 00:10:00,067
THIS ONE'S ON THE REBOUND.

252
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,903
AND NOW THE ONLY GIRL TO A
COMPLETE SUMMERSAULT

253
00:10:02,937 --> 00:10:05,072
TOO HIGH TO THE FEET
OF THE BALANCER.

254
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:08,175
THIS ACT WAS OUTLAWED
ON SEVERAL CONTINENTS.

255
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:11,145
HERE IS THE MAN WHO MISTOOK
HIS WIFE FOR A HAT.

256
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,850
- HI, RICK.
- SARAH.

257
00:10:16,883 --> 00:10:18,152
FLIPPED HER OFF.

258
00:10:18,185 --> 00:10:21,022
SORRY, WAYNE.
THIS IS FOR THE LADIES ONLY.

259
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:24,392
THE CELEBRATED
RIEFFENACH TROUPE,

260
00:10:24,425 --> 00:10:25,793
BAREBACK RIDING MARVELS

261
00:10:25,827 --> 00:10:27,728
WHOSE EQUALS DO NOT EXIST.

262
00:10:27,762 --> 00:10:29,997
GRACE AND BEAUTY
OF EQUESTRIANISM.

263
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:33,900
ON YOUR HEAD
IF YOU'RE SQUEAMISH.

264
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:35,368
YES, THIS ACT EMBODIES

265
00:10:35,402 --> 00:10:37,672
THE SADNESS THAT IS CIRCUS.

266
00:10:37,705 --> 00:10:40,775
- THAT IS TRUE, DOG.
- HEY, SORRY.

267
00:10:40,808 --> 00:10:41,808
WHAT? WHAT?

268
00:10:41,842 --> 00:10:43,710
IS ALL HE DOES IS EAT?

269
00:10:43,743 --> 00:10:45,780
- HE'S GOOD AT IT.
- WHAT?

270
00:10:45,813 --> 00:10:48,615
THE BEAUTIFUL BAREBACK RIDING
BALLERINA MISS LUCY.

271
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:50,050
COULD NOT BE WITH US
TONIGHT,

272
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:52,853
SO WE HAVE THIS ACT.

273
00:10:52,887 --> 00:10:54,355
YOU'RE NEXT UP THERE.

274
00:10:54,388 --> 00:10:56,690
AND NOW, LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

275
00:10:56,723 --> 00:11:00,627
- WE PRESENT THE...
- [LAUGHING]

276
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:04,132
WHOA, OH.
WHOO!

277
00:11:04,165 --> 00:11:06,633
UH. WHOA.

278
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:10,972
- WHOA. WHOA.
- I THOUGHT THAT WAS
ANOTHER BALL!

279
00:11:11,005 --> 00:11:12,607
HERE COME THE COMICS OF THE
AIR,

280
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:17,210
THE DEXTEROUS AND HILARIOUS
FEAT HIGH ABOVE THE... BAR.

281
00:11:17,243 --> 00:11:20,013
STORE THIS IMAGE AWAY
FOR A LATER NIGHTMARE.

282
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:26,220
- I INVENTED THAT MOVE.
- YEAH, RIGHT.

283
00:11:26,253 --> 00:11:28,988
LEVIS LOOSE-FITTING
CLOWN JEANS.

284
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,428
HUH?

285
00:11:34,462 --> 00:11:36,863
OH, NO, NO, NO.
THEY'RE DOING IT CLOWN STYLE.

286
00:11:36,897 --> 00:11:40,167
NO!

287
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,470
AND MADONNA THINKS
SHE'S INNOVATIVE.

288
00:11:42,503 --> 00:11:44,872
OH, PLEASE TELL ME
THIS ISN'T HAPPENING?

289
00:11:44,905 --> 00:11:47,675
OH, NO.

290
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:50,110
MORE, MORE.
I'M A BAD CLOWN.

291
00:11:50,143 --> 00:11:52,278
YES, CHILDREN'S WINDOWS
OF PERCEPTION

292
00:11:52,312 --> 00:11:53,713
ARE OPEN FOR ONLY A SECOND,

293
00:11:53,747 --> 00:11:56,983
ONLY TO TAKE IN THE HORROR
THAT IS THE CIRCUS.

294
00:11:57,017 --> 00:11:58,385
HIGH ABOVE THE CROWD,

295
00:11:58,418 --> 00:11:59,587
DAG HAMMARSKJOLD

296
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:02,623
TAKES TO THE TRAPEZE.

297
00:12:02,657 --> 00:12:07,227
YES, IT'S ALBERT SPEER NUDE
DONNING A DANCE BELT.

298
00:12:08,795 --> 00:12:10,397
IN THE CENTER RING,

299
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:14,000
THE ONLY GROUP OF PAMALINO
LIBERTY HORSES IN THE WORLD.

300
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:16,703
TAMED AND PRESENTED
BY ADOLF DELBOSS.

301
00:12:16,737 --> 00:12:18,505
WE WON'T LINGER ON THIS ONE,
FOLKS.

302
00:12:18,538 --> 00:12:21,575
THERE'S NOT MUCH TO IT,
REALLY.

303
00:12:21,608 --> 00:12:23,310
REMEMBER TO PUNCH IN, ED.

304
00:12:23,343 --> 00:12:26,013
[NEIGHS]

305
00:12:26,047 --> 00:12:28,215
- OH, THERE IS SIEGFRIED.
- OVER HERE, ROY.

306
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:29,583
- HELLO, SIEGFRIED.
- HELLO, ROY.

307
00:12:29,617 --> 00:12:31,018
YA YA.

308
00:12:32,285 --> 00:12:34,422
THIS IS A FREUDIAN DREAM.

309
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:41,228
HANK KIMBALL'S BROUGHT IN.

310
00:12:41,262 --> 00:12:42,930
HEY, MR. DOUGLAS.
SEE YOU GOT A HORSE.

311
00:12:42,963 --> 00:12:44,498
WELL, IT'S NOT REALLY A HORSE.
IT'S MORE OF A...

312
00:12:44,532 --> 00:12:48,635
UH, FELLAS,
THIS IS JUST WRONG.

313
00:12:48,668 --> 00:12:50,237
ON THE HIPPODROME TRACK,

314
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,473
HIGH-JUMPING HORSES.

315
00:12:52,507 --> 00:12:54,975
WHOO!

316
00:12:55,008 --> 00:12:57,343
EMMETT KELLY'S STILL EATING.

317
00:12:57,377 --> 00:13:01,182
AND IT'S STILL FUNNY.
[CHUCKLES]

318
00:13:01,215 --> 00:13:04,252
...WITH DOROTHY HERBERT
BLINDFOLDED OVER
A BARRIER OF FIRE.

319
00:13:04,285 --> 00:13:06,020
THAT'S BLACKENED BEAUTY,
THE CAJUN HORSE.

320
00:13:06,053 --> 00:13:07,688
IT'S C. EVERETT KOOK.

321
00:13:09,523 --> 00:13:13,760
...FOR THE FUNNIEST PRIZE FIGHT
IN CIRCUS HISTORY.

322
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:15,997
BING CROSBY'S RELATIONSHIP
WITH HIS SON GARY

323
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:18,998
IS RE-ENACTED.

324
00:13:19,032 --> 00:13:21,735
[CHUCKLES LIKE A CLOWN]
LET THE NIGHTMARE BEGIN.

325
00:13:21,768 --> 00:13:25,538
THIS IS THE STRANGEST DEBATE
FORMAT I HAVE EVER SEEN.

326
00:13:29,843 --> 00:13:31,178
YOU KNOW, DON'T LAUGH,
BUT IN A WAY

327
00:13:31,212 --> 00:13:33,213
THIS IS THIS TOWN'S
PASSION PLAY.

328
00:13:33,247 --> 00:13:37,150
OH, IT'S A FULL-CONTACT WHO'S
AFRAID OF VIRGINIA WOOLF.

329
00:13:37,183 --> 00:13:39,287
DON'T TALK ABOUT THAT CLOWN,
MARTHA.

330
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,955
- KITTIES!
- MEOW.

331
00:13:40,988 --> 00:13:42,255
AND NOW CLYDE BEATTY

332
00:13:42,288 --> 00:13:44,525
THE MOST FEARLESS MAN
IN ALL THE WORLD,

333
00:13:44,558 --> 00:13:45,758
ALONE IN A CAGE

334
00:13:45,792 --> 00:13:48,562
WITH A HERD OF MAN-EATING
AFRICAN LIONS.

335
00:13:48,595 --> 00:13:51,365
THE GREATEST WILD ANIMAL
TRAINER OF ALL TIME.

336
00:13:51,398 --> 00:13:56,237
IS NOT HERE.

337
00:13:56,270 --> 00:13:57,672
JOHN TURTURRO?

338
00:13:57,705 --> 00:14:02,008
HM?

339
00:14:02,042 --> 00:14:05,245
STELLA!

340
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,882
THE SIX FLYING THRILLERS,

341
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:10,150
DARING MID-AIR MARVELS

342
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:12,118
HIGH OVER THE CENTER RING,

343
00:14:12,152 --> 00:14:14,322
A TROUPE OF ABSOLUTELY
FEARLESS AND UNRIVALLED...

344
00:14:14,355 --> 00:14:16,257
LOOKS LIKE AN ANT FARM.

345
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:17,523
FLY THROUGH THE AIR,

346
00:14:17,558 --> 00:14:19,960
PERFORMING SPECTACULAR
AND HAZARDOUS FEATS.

347
00:14:19,993 --> 00:14:21,862
I KNOW. YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO COMPLETE 5TH-GRADE GYM

348
00:14:21,895 --> 00:14:24,265
WITHOUT DOING THIS, RIGHT?

349
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:25,565
COME ON.
LET ME HIT YOU ON THE BUTT.

350
00:14:25,598 --> 00:14:27,200
- NO.
- HOW ABOUT JUST A LIGHT TAP?

351
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:29,035
- UH-UH, NOT NOW.
- OH, COME ON, PLEASE.

352
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:30,570
LATER IT WILL BE
MUCH MORE FUN.

353
00:14:30,603 --> 00:14:32,472
- GUYS, STOP IT.
- YOU'RE RUINING IT FOR ME.

354
00:14:32,505 --> 00:14:34,342
WHAT? WHAT? SORRY.

355
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,948
PASS THE WORD.
ED'S BEEN HITTING
THE BOTTLE TODAY.

356
00:14:41,982 --> 00:14:43,683
OH, LIKE THAT'S
A BIG IMPROVEMENT

357
00:14:43,717 --> 00:14:44,785
OVER WHAT WE'VE BEEN DOING.

358
00:14:44,818 --> 00:14:47,220
PARTY IN SUSAN'S DRESSING ROOM.

359
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:48,988
[MUTTERS]

360
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,963
- UH-OH.
- IT'S JEAN ALLEN

361
00:14:55,997 --> 00:14:58,232
WITH A HERD OF THUNDEROUS
PACHYDERMS,

362
00:14:58,265 --> 00:15:01,002
THEIR TRUNKS
FULL OF NEW TRICKS.

363
00:15:01,035 --> 00:15:02,603
A ROGUE ELEPHANT
SNAPS ITS TETHER

364
00:15:02,637 --> 00:15:03,870
AND KILLS A COOLIE.

365
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,605
NOW WHO'S GETTING DARK?

366
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,007
HOO-HOO.

367
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,242
LIKE IT.

368
00:15:09,277 --> 00:15:14,180
I'M TAKING THIS ELEPHANT
FOR A TEST DRIVE.

369
00:15:14,213 --> 00:15:16,183
THREE ELEPHANTS
AND A LITTLE LADY.

370
00:15:19,018 --> 00:15:20,687
THE CIRCUS WITH IT'S THRILLS,

371
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,857
FUN, SAWDUST, AND SPANGLE

372
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:25,858
BRINGS JOY AND MERRIMENT
TO EVERYONE.

373
00:15:25,892 --> 00:15:27,327
HERE COMES THE CIRCUS

374
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,630
IS ALWAYS A MEMORABLE EVENT,

375
00:15:29,663 --> 00:15:32,298
A TRULY GREAT
AND CAREFREE DAY FOR ALL

376
00:15:32,332 --> 00:15:34,302
FROM SIX TO 60.

377
00:15:34,335 --> 00:15:36,270
YOU THINK SHE'S WORKING
FOR PEANUTS, TOO?

378
00:15:36,303 --> 00:15:40,773
[CHUCKLES]

379
00:15:40,807 --> 00:15:43,110
SHE ENJOYS THIS
A LITTLE TOO MUCH.

380
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:49,617
UM, DON'T BLOW
ANY WATER RIGHT NOW.

381
00:15:49,650 --> 00:15:51,918
AH, MY FAVORITE PART
OF THE CIRCUS.

382
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,597
OH, WAIT.
HOW CAN SOMETHING BE AMERICAN
AND INTERNATIONAL?

383
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,232
LET'S WATCH AND FIND OUT.
SHALL WE?

384
00:16:10,003 --> 00:16:12,038
OH, CRIPES,
I REMEMBER THAT DAY.

385
00:16:12,072 --> 00:16:13,540
OH, YEAH,
YOU GOTTA DRESS FOR IT.

386
00:16:13,573 --> 00:16:15,042
OH, YAHAY, THE TEMPERATURE--

387
00:16:15,075 --> 00:16:17,443
THAT GOT ALL THE WAY DOWN
TO ABOUT 14 BELOW ZERO THERE.

388
00:16:17,477 --> 00:16:19,813
- OH, YEAH.
- YOU DON'T KNOW
THE HALF OF IT.

389
00:16:19,847 --> 00:16:21,915
EARL HAD TO JUMP START
THE CHEVY THAT DAY.

390
00:16:21,948 --> 00:16:24,117
OH, YAHAY,
THE SNOW WAS YAY HIGH,

391
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:28,322
AND HE COME UP THE BACK WAY,
HE HAD TO. YOU KNOW?

392
00:16:28,355 --> 00:16:31,858
OF COURSE I DON'T KNOW
NOTHING ABOUT THAT.

393
00:16:31,892 --> 00:16:36,063
THEN WE SEEN WHERE
ALL THE SCHOOLS IS CLOSED.

394
00:16:36,097 --> 00:16:37,765
OF COURSE THE KIDS
ENJOYED THAT PART.

395
00:16:37,798 --> 00:16:39,132
THAT WAS REAL COLD, YEAH.

396
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:40,967
IT WAS JUST LIKE
THE WINTER OF '75,

397
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,770
WHEN IT GOT DOWN TO 30 BELOW.

398
00:16:42,803 --> 00:16:44,972
OH, YEAH, BUT WHEN YOU
CONSIDER THE WIND CHILL,

399
00:16:45,005 --> 00:16:46,973
IT'S WHEN IT'S ABOUT A HUNDRED
BELOW THAT TIME.

400
00:16:47,007 --> 00:16:48,308
OH, JOEL, YOU KNOW

401
00:16:48,342 --> 00:16:49,777
IT WAS A GOOD THING I HAD
THE SNOWMOBILE SUIT

402
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:51,378
FOR THE RUN OVER
BY EVELYN'S HOUSE THERE.

403
00:16:51,412 --> 00:16:53,347
OH, SURE. YEP, YEP.

404
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,048
IT WAS JUST SO DING DANG COLD,

405
00:16:55,082 --> 00:16:58,685
I GO OUTSIDE,
THE STUFF IN MY NOSE
JUST FREEZE RIGHT UP.

406
00:16:58,718 --> 00:17:00,587
AH, YEP, YEP.

407
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:02,455
AH, THE SCANDIHOOVIAN SKETCH.
YEAH.

408
00:17:02,488 --> 00:17:05,092
OH, YAH, SQUAREHEAD.

409
00:17:08,795 --> 00:17:10,063
THROUGHOUT HISTORY

410
00:17:10,097 --> 00:17:11,598
PEOPLE HAVE LISTENED
TO THE STORYTELLER.

411
00:17:11,632 --> 00:17:12,967
AGAINST THEIR WILL.

412
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,568
MEN WHO COULD FASHION
MYTHS AND FAIRYTALES

413
00:17:15,602 --> 00:17:18,138
AND MAKE THEM LIVE
FOR HIS LISTENERS.

414
00:17:18,172 --> 00:17:19,640
SID AND MARTY KROFFT?

415
00:17:19,673 --> 00:17:21,475
SUCH MEN WERE THE BROTHERS
GRIMM IN GERMANY

416
00:17:21,508 --> 00:17:24,210
AND HANS CHRISTIAN ANDERSEN
IN DENMARK,

417
00:17:24,243 --> 00:17:27,882
AND SUCH A MAN
WAS ELIAS LONNROT IN FINLAND.

418
00:17:27,915 --> 00:17:29,282
HERE HE IS ON VACATION.

419
00:17:29,315 --> 00:17:30,983
THIS IS THE STORY
YOU ARE ABOUT TO SEE.

420
00:17:31,017 --> 00:17:31,985
AAH!

421
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:33,953
PHEW.

422
00:17:33,987 --> 00:17:37,390
- THEY'RE GOLEM.
- LONG AGO IN A FARAWAY PLACE
CALLED KALEVALA

423
00:17:37,423 --> 00:17:39,560
THERE WAS A VILLAGE
OF FISHER PEOPLE.

424
00:17:39,593 --> 00:17:42,495
THE LAND THEY LIVED IN
WAS LARGE AND BEAUTIFUL.

425
00:17:42,528 --> 00:17:43,763
AS WERE THE WOMEN.

426
00:17:43,797 --> 00:17:45,098
...BLESSED WITH GREAT RIVERS

427
00:17:45,132 --> 00:17:46,867
FILLED WITH FISH,

428
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:49,570
WONDERFUL FORESTS
WITH TALL TREES...

429
00:17:49,603 --> 00:17:52,272
AND POLLUTION FROM THE NEARBY
PAPER PROCESSING PLANT.

430
00:17:52,305 --> 00:17:54,407
AND THE PEOPLE TOILED
VERY HARD.

431
00:17:54,442 --> 00:17:56,443
HEY, THIS IS HARD.

432
00:17:56,477 --> 00:17:58,245
...AND IF THEY WORKED
THE EARTH AND THE SEA...

433
00:17:58,278 --> 00:17:59,580
BYE, GRANDMA.

434
00:17:59,613 --> 00:18:02,850
...ONE DAY THEY WOULD BE GIVEN
AS THEIR REWARD...

435
00:18:02,883 --> 00:18:04,752
IS THIS A DOCUMENTARY?

436
00:18:04,785 --> 00:18:07,720
I'M HERE FOR THE PRINCE VALIANT
AUDITIONS.

437
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:11,325
♪♪ [HUMS "DUELING BANJOS"]

438
00:18:11,358 --> 00:18:13,360
ONE, TWO, THREE--

439
00:18:13,393 --> 00:18:15,195
I CAN'T FALL ASLEEP
COUNTING THOSE GUYS.

440
00:18:15,228 --> 00:18:16,230
GOATS.

441
00:18:16,263 --> 00:18:17,730
OH.

442
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:21,835
...AND SO SUCH WAS THE MAGIC
OF THE SAMPO...

443
00:18:21,868 --> 00:18:23,103
THE WHAT?

444
00:18:23,137 --> 00:18:24,505
IT SO HAPPENED
THAT THE ILLMARINEN

445
00:18:24,538 --> 00:18:26,373
HAD A BEAUTIFUL SISTER
NAMED ANNIKKI...

446
00:18:26,407 --> 00:18:28,075
"ANNIKKI IN THE U.K."?

447
00:18:28,108 --> 00:18:29,275
HUH.

448
00:18:29,308 --> 00:18:30,877
...AND SPENT HER DAYS
HAPPILY...

449
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:33,080
YOUR MOTHER IS LONG DEAD.

450
00:18:33,113 --> 00:18:35,548
ALL THE PEOPLE OF THE VILLAGE
LOVED HER DEARLY

451
00:18:35,582 --> 00:18:38,152
HEY, THERE'S BIRD LANCASTER.

452
00:18:38,185 --> 00:18:40,120
WALTER PIDGEON.
ROBIN GIVENS.

453
00:18:40,153 --> 00:18:41,788
- CHICK COREA.
- OOH, GOOD ONE.

454
00:18:41,822 --> 00:18:43,323
...THAT WOULD BE THE SIGN

455
00:18:43,357 --> 00:18:44,925
THAT THE TIME HAD COME...

456
00:18:44,958 --> 00:18:46,193
FOR DEMOCRACY.

457
00:18:46,227 --> 00:18:47,693
SAMPO WAS TO BE FORGED.

458
00:18:47,727 --> 00:18:49,095
ESCAPE TO WISCONSIN.

459
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:51,265
EVER SINCE ANNIKKI
HAD BECOME A YOUNG WOMAN,

460
00:18:51,298 --> 00:18:53,933
SHE REMAINED BY HERSELF

461
00:18:53,967 --> 00:18:56,270
AND REFUSED THE ATTENTION
OF ANY YOUNG MAN

462
00:18:56,303 --> 00:18:57,637
WHO BRAZENLY THOUGHT
HE MIGHT...

463
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,873
LOOK AT THAT.
LOOKS LIKE PENNY MARSHALL.

464
00:18:59,907 --> 00:19:01,908
...ONE MAN SHE HAD NEVER MET...

465
00:19:01,942 --> 00:19:03,043
GARY BIGNER.

466
00:19:03,077 --> 00:19:05,045
...FOR HE LIVED DEEPER
IN THE FOREST.

467
00:19:05,078 --> 00:19:07,480
HIS NAME WAS LEMMINKAINEN.

468
00:19:07,513 --> 00:19:08,682
LIME LEMMINKAINEN.

469
00:19:08,715 --> 00:19:09,950
HE WAS A WOODSMAN.

470
00:19:09,983 --> 00:19:11,652
HE WAS YOUNG AND SIMPLE.

471
00:19:11,685 --> 00:19:14,020
AND PRACTICED SLASH-AND-BURN
AGRICULTURE.

472
00:19:14,053 --> 00:19:15,788
- HE WORKED HARD--
- [ALL] OHH!

473
00:19:15,822 --> 00:19:17,790
- ...BUT WAS NEVER NOTICED
AT ALL.
- WHEW.

474
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:20,860
- BUT THERE WAS SOMETHING
ABOUT HIM THAT WOULD SOMEDAY--
- [GRUNTING]

475
00:19:20,893 --> 00:19:23,063
- OH, THERE GOES THE LAST
SPOTTED OWL.
- ...SOONER THAN ANYONE THOUGHT,

476
00:19:23,097 --> 00:19:25,532
SAVE THE VILLAGE
FROM THE MOST HORRIBLE, CRUEL

477
00:19:25,565 --> 00:19:27,467
MISFORTUNE IT WOULD EVER KNOW.

478
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,102
- THE REAGAN-BUSH
ADMINISTRATION.
- WHAT THESE GOOD PEOPLE

479
00:19:29,135 --> 00:19:32,705
DID NOT REALIZE:
THAT ALL THE TIME--

480
00:19:32,738 --> 00:19:34,708
HAS ANYONE SEEN TIMMY?
OH, NO!

481
00:19:34,742 --> 00:19:36,877
...A WITCH
PLOTTED AGAINST THEM.

482
00:19:36,910 --> 00:19:38,845
HEY, CHECK IT OUT.
IT'S STING

483
00:19:38,878 --> 00:19:40,913
AND DAVID LEE ROTH
AND PETER NOONE

484
00:19:40,947 --> 00:19:43,617
AND SAMMY HAGAR
AND DAVID CARRADINE AND...

485
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:46,052
- SANTA?
- HMM.

486
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:52,525
WHY DON'T YOU USE AN AX
ON YOUR HAIR, YOU HIPPIE?

487
00:19:52,558 --> 00:19:55,828
FOR THREE DAYS,
YOUR MOTHER HAS NOT SEEN YOU,
LEMMINKAINEN.

488
00:19:55,862 --> 00:19:58,165
- GO HOME AND TAKE A REST.
- AND TAKE OUT THE GARBAGE,

489
00:19:58,198 --> 00:20:01,235
AND HELP YOUR MOTHER
CLEAN THE GARAGE,
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

490
00:20:01,268 --> 00:20:03,037
[CLAPPING A TUNE]

491
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:05,872
♪ FROM THE LAND
OF SKY-BLUE WATER ♪

492
00:20:05,905 --> 00:20:08,908
♪ WATER ♪

493
00:20:08,942 --> 00:20:11,545
HEY, CHECK OUT MY LOG.
I GOT IT FOR GRADUATION.

494
00:20:11,578 --> 00:20:13,547
[CHUCKLES]
IT'S MY CIGAR BOAT.

495
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,082
[LAUGHING]

496
00:20:15,115 --> 00:20:18,318
- AND A RIVER RUNS THROUGH IT.
- OR THIS.

497
00:20:18,352 --> 00:20:22,755
HEY, GET ME, I'M MAKING
A MOUNTAIN DEW AD.

498
00:20:22,788 --> 00:20:26,192
♪ LET'S GO SURFIN' NOW,
EVEN SVEN'S LEARNIN' HOW ♪

499
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:29,697
♪ IF EVERYBODY HAD A SPRUCE TREE
ACROSS FINLANDIA ♪

500
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:32,698
♪ I WISH THEY ALL COULD BE
NORWEGIAN GIRLS ♪

501
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:34,333
♪ THEY ALL COULD BE ♪

502
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:36,670
[MOCK FOREIGN ACCENT]
HEY, ANYBODY CALL A CAB?

503
00:20:36,703 --> 00:20:38,972
THE ADVENTURES
OF FJORD FAIRLANE.

504
00:20:39,005 --> 00:20:40,707
[LAUGHTER]

505
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:44,277
UH-OH. RUSH HOUR.

506
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:46,547
NOW, WAIT A MINUTE.
LET ME GET THIS STRAIGHT.

507
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:49,382
ABBA'S GONNA PAY ME TO SURF?

508
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:51,485
JOHN HUSTON'S THE AFRICAN LOG.

509
00:20:51,518 --> 00:20:54,253
WHITE HUNTER, BLACK HEART.

510
00:20:54,287 --> 00:20:56,188
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
DAMN, CRAZY SWEDE.

511
00:20:57,657 --> 00:20:59,525
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
ANCIENT SWEDISH SECRET, HUH?

512
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:01,528
♪ MY BABY TAKES-- ♪
HUH?

513
00:21:01,562 --> 00:21:03,797
WOW. LOOK AT THAT LAUNDRY.

514
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,365
[MOCK CHUCKLING]

515
00:21:08,068 --> 00:21:10,537
HEY, I'M GONNA GO PLAY MINI GOLF
AT CROSS LAKE.

516
00:21:10,570 --> 00:21:12,372
YOU WANNA GO?

517
00:21:12,405 --> 00:21:14,540
SHE'S WASHING HER CRYSTAL.

518
00:21:14,573 --> 00:21:16,042
HMM?

519
00:21:16,075 --> 00:21:18,978
DON'T WALK ON MY LAUNDRY,
STEVE.

520
00:21:22,748 --> 00:21:26,218
YES? MAY I HELP YOU?

521
00:21:27,687 --> 00:21:29,990
- WHOSE GOLD IS THAT?
- MINE.

522
00:21:30,023 --> 00:21:31,792
[LEMMINKAINEN]
CAN THIS BE THE DAUGHTER
OF THE ROSY DAWN?

523
00:21:31,825 --> 00:21:34,293
[WHISPERING]
AGENT, HE'S JUST PULLED UP
IN A LOG.

524
00:21:34,327 --> 00:21:36,530
[LEMMINKAINEN]
OR THE RADIANCE OF THE MOON?

525
00:21:36,563 --> 00:21:40,733
IT'S NOT THE MOON,
NOR IS IT THE SUN.

526
00:21:40,767 --> 00:21:42,835
I'M JUST A SIMPLE MAIDEN.

527
00:21:42,868 --> 00:21:44,337
YOU CAN SAY THAT AGAIN.

528
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:47,707
- ANNIKKI IS MY NAME.
- POKER'S MY GAME.

529
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:50,143
- ANNIKKI.
- I WENT TO SCHOOL
WITH YOUR BROTHER.

530
00:21:50,177 --> 00:21:52,978
HEY, MY OTHER LOG'S A REDWOOD.

531
00:21:53,013 --> 00:21:54,613
- [LAUGHTER]
- SHE'S GOT A GUN!

532
00:21:54,647 --> 00:21:56,683
- [ALL YELL]
- OH.

533
00:21:56,717 --> 00:21:59,118
[OLD MAN'S VOICE]
IF YOU DON'T LIKE
THE WAY I'M DRIVING,

534
00:21:59,152 --> 00:22:02,188
CALL 1-800-BITE-ME.
[LAUGHS]

535
00:22:02,222 --> 00:22:04,157
[FOREIGN ACCENT]
WELL, IT WAS NICE MEETING YOU.

536
00:22:04,190 --> 00:22:06,360
"LEMMINKAINEN," WAS IT?
EH, WHATEVER.

537
00:22:06,393 --> 00:22:08,428
[IMITATING VEHICLE DEPARTING]

538
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:12,032
THAT WAS WEIRD.

539
00:22:12,065 --> 00:22:15,368
DO YOU WANT TO BE FINNISH?
SURE. WE ALL DO.

540
00:22:15,402 --> 00:22:17,737
♪♪ [HUMMING]

541
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:20,240
POPPIES WILL MAKE US SLEEP.

542
00:22:20,273 --> 00:22:22,042
- [WHISPERING] THEY'RE TULIPS.
- OH.

543
00:22:22,075 --> 00:22:26,112
[IMITATING FROGS CROAKING]

544
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:33,253
AH, YES, MY LITTLE CHICKADEE.

545
00:22:33,287 --> 00:22:36,055
HEY, WHAT'S
THE PECKING ORDER HERE?
[LAUGHS]

546
00:22:36,088 --> 00:22:37,623
EH...

547
00:22:37,657 --> 00:22:42,028
SHE'S GOT AN AMAZINGLY
DULL LIFE, DOESN'T SHE?

548
00:22:42,062 --> 00:22:45,432
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
AH, DINNER.

549
00:22:45,465 --> 00:22:48,202
- OH, NO, AFTER YOU.
- NO, AFTER YOU. I INSIST.

550
00:22:48,235 --> 00:22:50,403
- NO, I INSIST.
AGE BEFORE BEAUTY.
- OH, N--

551
00:22:50,437 --> 00:22:53,140
[IMITATING YOGI BEAR]
HEY, HELLO, BOO-BOO. MMM.

552
00:22:53,173 --> 00:22:55,875
JOHN IRVING
WROTE THE SCREENPLAY.

553
00:22:58,245 --> 00:23:02,215
I'M BUSY.

554
00:23:02,248 --> 00:23:05,018
ANNIKKI.

555
00:23:05,052 --> 00:23:06,118
SISTER OF MINE.

556
00:23:06,152 --> 00:23:07,287
YOU SHAVED YOUR BEARD.

557
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,322
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

558
00:23:08,355 --> 00:23:10,790
OH, MY DEAREST BROTHER.

559
00:23:10,823 --> 00:23:13,093
HIS EYES SPARKLE
LIKE THE SUNLIGHT

560
00:23:13,127 --> 00:23:14,593
GLIMMERING ON THE SEA FOAM.

561
00:23:14,627 --> 00:23:17,597
[LAUGHS]

562
00:23:27,607 --> 00:23:28,908
YES!

563
00:23:28,942 --> 00:23:30,910
AND THEN WE SWING
BACK AND FORTH ON THE HIGHWIRE

564
00:23:30,943 --> 00:23:32,645
WHILE FURIOUSLY
SPANKING EACH OTHER.

565
00:23:32,678 --> 00:23:35,115
GREAT! I LOVE IT!
IT SINGS. IT'S GOT LEGS.

566
00:23:35,148 --> 00:23:36,148
IT'S GOT EVERYTHING--

567
00:23:36,182 --> 00:23:38,218
LISTEN, YOU GUYS.
PLEASE.

568
00:23:38,252 --> 00:23:39,452
REMEMBER I SAID I'D TYPE IN

569
00:23:39,485 --> 00:23:41,722
YOUR IDEAS FOR A CLOWN ACT,
ALL RIGHT?

570
00:23:41,755 --> 00:23:43,590
I FIND WHAT
WE'RE TALKING ABOUT HERE

571
00:23:43,623 --> 00:23:44,892
JUST A LITTLE BIT DERIVATIVE

572
00:23:44,925 --> 00:23:47,360
FROM WHAT WE SAW THE CLOWNS
DO IN THE SHORT.

573
00:23:47,393 --> 00:23:49,362
I THINK YOU SHOULD
THINK OF YOUR OWN IDEAS.

574
00:23:49,395 --> 00:23:51,097
WELL, WE'RE NOT
PAYING YOU TO THINK.

575
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:53,467
JUST TAKE ALL THIS DOWN
AS WE DICTATE IT, PEGGY.

576
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:55,002
OKAY.
WHERE WERE WE?

577
00:23:55,035 --> 00:23:56,970
WAIT. I'VE GOT IT.

578
00:23:57,003 --> 00:23:58,905
- WE'RE ON THE TRAPEZE.
- YEP.

579
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:01,307
AND YOU HANG FROM MY TONGUE.

580
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:03,577
WHILE I DRIVE SHEET-METAL
SCREWS INTO YOUR EYES.

581
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:04,610
I LOVE IT!

582
00:24:04,643 --> 00:24:06,412
IT'S GOOD.
I ADMIT THAT.

583
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:08,382
BUT MAYBE WE GOTTA WORK
MORE BUTT INTO THE ACT.

584
00:24:08,415 --> 00:24:10,317
- WAIT, I'VE GOT IT.
- YEAH?

585
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:12,418
I GRAB YOU AND SQUEEZE YOU
TILL YOU HEMORRHAGE--

586
00:24:12,452 --> 00:24:14,753
NO, HOW ABOUT I COME OUT
DRESSED AS A SUTURE,

587
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:16,823
YOU COME OUT
DRESSED AS AN APPENDIX.

588
00:24:16,857 --> 00:24:18,858
A EUROPEAN APPENDIX,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

589
00:24:18,892 --> 00:24:19,893
OOH, VERY KINKY.

590
00:24:19,927 --> 00:24:21,093
UH, FELLAS,
CAN I REMIND YOU,

591
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:22,728
YOU'RE GONNA BE CLOWNS
IN A CIRCUS.

592
00:24:22,762 --> 00:24:24,430
THERE'S GONNA BE
KIDS WATCHING.

593
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:26,667
CAN I JUST REMIND YOU
TO BITE ME?

594
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:28,335
NOW GET BACK TO WORK, DELLA.

595
00:24:28,368 --> 00:24:30,837
RIGHT!
I'VE GOT A BRILLIANT IDEA!

596
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:31,872
OKAY.

597
00:24:31,905 --> 00:24:33,873
THIS ROUTINE
STARTS OUT NORMAL,

598
00:24:33,907 --> 00:24:36,308
YOU AND ME BEATING THE CRAP
OUT OF EACH OTHER.

599
00:24:36,342 --> 00:24:37,477
THEN I SNAP.

600
00:24:37,510 --> 00:24:39,245
I RUN INTO THE AUDIENCE
ON A HOMICIDAL RAMPAGE.

601
00:24:39,278 --> 00:24:40,480
HA HA!

602
00:24:40,513 --> 00:24:42,315
YES. THEN I APPEAR
PLAYING THE PART OF DEATH.

603
00:24:42,348 --> 00:24:43,883
A FUNNY DEATH.
OF COURSE.

604
00:24:43,917 --> 00:24:45,918
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT WOULD BE
A REALLY FUNNY ROUTINE?

605
00:24:45,952 --> 00:24:47,053
WHAT WOULD BE REALLY FUNNY?

606
00:24:47,087 --> 00:24:48,688
IF WE COULD SOMEHOW MAKE
THE AUDIENCE MEMBERS

607
00:24:48,722 --> 00:24:50,723
QUESTION THEIR LOVE
FOR THEIR SPOUSES.

608
00:24:50,757 --> 00:24:52,192
YES, AND HERE'S THE TOPPER.

609
00:24:52,225 --> 00:24:53,827
WE CONVINCE ALL THE KIDS
IN THE AUDIENCE

610
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:54,862
THAT THEY WERE ADOPTED!

611
00:24:54,895 --> 00:24:56,530
AH, HA HA!

612
00:24:56,563 --> 00:24:57,797
GUYS, LISTEN.

613
00:24:57,830 --> 00:24:59,900
I KNEW YOU WOULD TAKE
SOMETHING LIKE THE CIRCUS

614
00:24:59,933 --> 00:25:02,768
AND TURN IT INTO SOME DARK
CARNIVAL OF THE SOUL.

615
00:25:02,802 --> 00:25:04,637
LISTEN, JOEL,
FOR YOUR INFORMATION--

616
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,138
- WHAT THE HELL?
- HEY!

617
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:07,707
YOU DIDN'T TAKE DOWN
A WORD WE SAID!

618
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:10,443
YOU HAD CAMBOT PROGRAM
A TYPING EFFECT.

619
00:25:10,477 --> 00:25:12,478
YOU WERE JUST TOYING WITH US,
WEREN'T YOU?

620
00:25:12,512 --> 00:25:14,780
- THAT'S RIGHT.
AND YOU KNOW WHY?
- WHY?

621
00:25:14,813 --> 00:25:17,417
BECAUSE THERE'S A LITTLE BIT
OF THE CLOWN IN ALL OF US.

622
00:25:17,450 --> 00:25:19,352
GOOD NIGHT,
AND MAY GOD BLESS.

623
00:25:19,385 --> 00:25:21,087
[ROBOTS SCOFFING]

624
00:25:27,193 --> 00:25:30,563
- OH, COME ON.
I COULDN'T RESIST.
- YEAH. WHATEVER.

625
00:25:30,597 --> 00:25:34,400
THIS WAS BEFORE UNIONS.
LET IT BE A LESSON TO YOU.

626
00:25:34,433 --> 00:25:37,103
HEY, TOM,
COULD YOU PUNCH OUT FOR ME?

627
00:25:37,137 --> 00:25:39,538
[MAN SHOUTING]

628
00:25:39,572 --> 00:25:42,342
I'M NOT GOING INTO
EARLY RETIREMENT.

629
00:25:42,375 --> 00:25:44,743
RON WOOD ON
ANY GIVEN MORNING.

630
00:25:44,777 --> 00:25:46,647
OOH.

631
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:48,415
YOU'VE COME FOR THE FIRE.

632
00:25:48,448 --> 00:25:50,183
COME ON.
A TOUR'S COMING THROUGH HERE.

633
00:25:50,217 --> 00:25:51,985
GET TO WORK!

634
00:25:52,018 --> 00:25:54,453
- YOU'VE COME FOR THE FIRES.
- HMM?

635
00:25:54,487 --> 00:25:56,255
HOW MUCH LONGER DO YOU
EXPECT ME TO PUT UP

636
00:25:56,288 --> 00:25:58,458
WITH YOUR ABSURD SHOW?

637
00:25:58,492 --> 00:26:01,828
CAN'T YOU MAKE THE SAMPO?
YOU CALL YOURSELVES WIZARDS!

638
00:26:01,862 --> 00:26:03,963
- DUH...
- WE'VE DONE THE BEST
WE'RE ABLE TO.

639
00:26:03,997 --> 00:26:06,767
- CAST THEM INTO
THE VIPER'S PIT!
- UH, BE UNCLEAN, MA'AM.

640
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,768
LET THE SNAKES DEVOUR HIM.

641
00:26:08,802 --> 00:26:10,437
CAN'T YOU JUST DOCK ME?

642
00:26:10,470 --> 00:26:13,172
OH, MISTRESS, I BEG OF YOU.

643
00:26:13,205 --> 00:26:14,773
I KNOW SOMEONE
WHO WILL BE ABLE TO HELP YOU

644
00:26:14,807 --> 00:26:16,610
TO BUILD YOUR SAMPO.

645
00:26:16,643 --> 00:26:20,180
- WHO?
- MURRAY ON THIRD SHIFT.

646
00:26:20,213 --> 00:26:23,750
...ILLMARINEN,
IN THE LAND OF KALEVALA.

647
00:26:23,783 --> 00:26:26,485
HE IS THE ONLY ONE
WHO KNOWS THE RIGHT WAY.

648
00:26:26,518 --> 00:26:29,588
YOU... HAVE LONG BOASTED

649
00:26:29,622 --> 00:26:32,258
OF YOUR POWER
OVER THE SECRETS OF NATURE.

650
00:26:32,292 --> 00:26:33,793
I DEMAND THAT YOU
SHOW ME NOW

651
00:26:33,827 --> 00:26:37,297
THE FACE OF THIS ILLMARINEN.

652
00:26:37,330 --> 00:26:39,665
MMM, LET'S GO CHECK
THE FILES, HONEY.

653
00:26:39,698 --> 00:26:43,770
[LAUGHS]
DON'T KNOW WHAT I'D DO
WITHOUT MY RIGHT-HAND TROLL.

654
00:26:43,803 --> 00:26:45,538
GESUNDHEIT.
GESUNDHEIT.
GESUNDHEIT.

655
00:26:45,572 --> 00:26:49,108
ILLMARINEN, COME BEFORE US.
ILLMARINEN, STAND BEFORE US.

656
00:26:49,142 --> 00:26:50,910
- COME BEFORE US,
STAND BEFORE US.
- OH, THEY'RE PENTECOSTAL.

657
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:52,312
ILLMARINEN, COME BEFORE US.

658
00:26:52,345 --> 00:26:55,482
- ILLMARINEN, STAND BEFORE US.
- POSTURE.

659
00:26:55,515 --> 00:26:58,217
- HE'S LEAKING.
- ILLMARINEN, COME BEFORE US.
ILLMARINEN, STAND BEFORE US.

660
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,818
- ILLMARINEN!
- APPEAR!

661
00:26:59,852 --> 00:27:01,822
HELP ME, OBI-WAN.
YOU'RE MY ONLY HELP.

662
00:27:01,855 --> 00:27:05,425
HEY, DON'T SIT SO CLOSE
TO THE SET.
YOU'LL RUIN OUR EYES.

663
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:07,960
I HAVE FASHIONED A BRACELET
FOR YOU.

664
00:27:07,993 --> 00:27:10,663
IT'S A PADLOCK!

665
00:27:10,697 --> 00:27:13,500
- ANNIKKI?
- NO, PRECIOUS MOMENTS.

666
00:27:13,533 --> 00:27:16,670
AND SHE IS
ILLMARINEN'S SISTER.

667
00:27:16,703 --> 00:27:19,605
OH, NO WAY. I THOUGHT SHE WAS
JOANIE KOSLACK'S BROTHER.

668
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:22,042
...WILL BE PAID
FOR HIS PRETTY SISTER.

669
00:27:22,075 --> 00:27:25,078
I WONDER WHAT KIND OF NAME
LEMMINKäINEN IS.

670
00:27:25,112 --> 00:27:26,578
ITALIAN? IRISH?

671
00:27:26,612 --> 00:27:28,382
♪ LEMMINKäINEN VERY PRETTY ♪

672
00:27:28,415 --> 00:27:31,050
[LAUGHS]
I MADE A JOKE.

673
00:27:31,083 --> 00:27:34,920
GO ON SWIFT WINGS
TO THE LAND OF KALEVALA.

674
00:27:34,953 --> 00:27:37,290
OH, ONE-HOUR MARTINIZING.

675
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:39,592
...TO THE GOLDEN ANNIKKI.

676
00:27:39,625 --> 00:27:43,430
WHEN YOU FIND HER ALONE,
BRING HER QUICKLY BACK

677
00:27:43,463 --> 00:27:46,700
SO THAT SHE MAY BECOME
MY PRISONER!

678
00:27:46,733 --> 00:27:49,535
OH, SHE'S ONE SHEET
TO THE WIND.

679
00:27:49,568 --> 00:27:52,638
OH, WAIT A MINUTE.
I FORGOT SOMETHING. OH!

680
00:27:52,672 --> 00:27:54,540
GRANDMA'S BEEN TALKING
TO THE BEDDING AGAIN.

681
00:27:54,573 --> 00:27:55,875
CUCKOO, CUCKOO.

682
00:27:55,908 --> 00:27:59,112
YOU REALLY GET A LOT OF USE
OUT OF A GOOD WOOL CAPE.

683
00:27:59,145 --> 00:28:03,248
WE'LL BE CRUISING TODAY
AT AN ALTITUDE
OF ABOUT 60 FEET OR SO.

684
00:28:04,483 --> 00:28:06,518
WELL, LET'S SEE.
NOW, WHAT DID SHE SAY?

685
00:28:06,552 --> 00:28:09,088
GO TO SOMETHING
AND GET SOMETHING, UH...

686
00:28:09,122 --> 00:28:10,790
- SOMETHING.
- [MUTTERS]

687
00:28:10,823 --> 00:28:13,927
YEAH, PLEASE REMAIN SEATED
UNTIL THE CAPE HAS COME
TO A COMPLETE STOP.

688
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:15,895
- THANK YOU.
- HMM?

689
00:28:15,928 --> 00:28:17,963
OH, DON'T TELL ME HERCULES
IS IN THIS MOVIE.

690
00:28:17,997 --> 00:28:20,867
- HERCULES IS IN THIS MOVIE.
- I ASKED YOU NOT
TO TELL ME THAT.

691
00:28:20,900 --> 00:28:22,768
♪ OH, THE CABIN BOY,
THE CABIN BOY ♪

692
00:28:22,802 --> 00:28:25,972
- ♪ THE DIRTY LITTLE... ♪
♪♪ [HUMMING]
- [WHISPERING] NO. NO.

693
00:28:28,073 --> 00:28:29,475
HMM?

694
00:28:31,077 --> 00:28:34,613
- HEY, UH, HOW'D I DO THAT?
- YEAH.

695
00:28:34,647 --> 00:28:38,150
- [WIND HOWLING]
- BOY, KIDNAPPING WAS REAL EASY
BACK THEN.

696
00:28:38,183 --> 00:28:40,153
OH-HO, POPEYE!

697
00:28:40,187 --> 00:28:41,487
♪ HE'S LARGE ♪

698
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:44,023
♪♪ [HUMMING]
WHAT THE HELL?

699
00:28:45,092 --> 00:28:47,060
THERE'S A ROAST IN THE OVEN!

700
00:28:47,093 --> 00:28:49,828
I DON'T KNOW
WHEN I'LL BE BACK!

701
00:28:52,065 --> 00:28:54,733
OH, BOY.

702
00:28:54,767 --> 00:28:57,337
THE SECRET STORM!

703
00:28:58,705 --> 00:29:01,140
♪ "DA" "VEATHER" STARTED
GETTIN' ROUGH ♪

704
00:29:01,173 --> 00:29:03,108
♪ THE TINY SHIP "VAS" LOST ♪

705
00:29:05,010 --> 00:29:08,213
THERE'S A FLASH FLOOD WARNING
AFFECTING STONEHENGE REGION.

706
00:29:08,247 --> 00:29:09,582
RIGHT.

707
00:29:12,318 --> 00:29:14,253
[HAG VOICE]
BY THE PRICKING OF MY THUMB,

708
00:29:14,287 --> 00:29:17,257
SOMETHING GOOFY
THIS WAY COMES.

709
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:18,925
[CHUCKLING]

710
00:29:20,893 --> 00:29:22,795
COME ON, DUMMY.

711
00:29:24,163 --> 00:29:25,665
♪♪ [HUMMING ALONG
WITH SOUNDTRACK]

712
00:29:25,698 --> 00:29:28,568
GEEZ, THANKS FOR THE LIFT.

713
00:29:28,602 --> 00:29:31,938
CALL THE FRONT DESK
IF YOU NEED ANYTHING.

714
00:29:34,273 --> 00:29:35,642
[LAUGHS]

715
00:29:35,675 --> 00:29:37,843
I GOT ONE!

716
00:29:39,612 --> 00:29:42,048
HEY, GET ME. I'M SWEDISH,
AND I'VE GOT RHYTHM.

717
00:29:42,082 --> 00:29:44,417
♪ I SING WHENEVER I SING ♪

718
00:29:44,450 --> 00:29:45,652
[LAUGHING]

719
00:29:45,685 --> 00:29:48,387
- ILLMARINEN!
- IT'S 3:00 IN THE MORNING!

720
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:51,157
THE EVIL WITCH LOUHI
HAS STOLEN YOUR SISTER.

721
00:29:51,190 --> 00:29:52,425
YEAH? AND?

722
00:29:52,458 --> 00:29:54,593
- ANNIKKI?
- YES.

723
00:29:54,627 --> 00:29:56,595
HERE. WAIT A MINUTE.
LET ME PUT MY SWORD OUT.

724
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:58,598
THERE.

725
00:29:58,632 --> 00:30:00,933
GIVE ME THE SWORD.

726
00:30:00,967 --> 00:30:03,368
I WILL GO TO POHJOLA.

727
00:30:04,770 --> 00:30:07,273
AH, LET ME JUST FINISH UP HERE.

728
00:30:07,307 --> 00:30:09,742
SO THERE.

729
00:30:09,775 --> 00:30:11,810
SAY HI TO MY SISTER.

730
00:30:11,845 --> 00:30:14,647
I WILL GO WITH YOU TO POHJOLA,
LEMMINKäINEN.

731
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,883
WAIT. I'LL DRIVE.
LET ME GET MY KEYS.

732
00:30:16,917 --> 00:30:19,852
YEP. THERE WE GO.
♪♪ [HUMMING]

733
00:30:21,855 --> 00:30:24,690
VAINAMOINEN,
MY SISTER HAS BEEN STOLEN--

734
00:30:24,723 --> 00:30:27,827
- WELL, WAS SHE INSURED?
- ...BY THE EVIL WITCH LOUHI.

735
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:30,497
- LOOKS KIND OF LIKE
A BIBLE STORY.
- YEAH.

736
00:30:30,530 --> 00:30:33,667
TELL US HOW WE CAN FIND OUR WAY
TO THE MYSTERY SHORES
OF POHJOLA.

737
00:30:33,700 --> 00:30:35,835
- GO DOWN TO
THE THIRD STOPLIGHT, AND...
- ALL THE WAY

738
00:30:35,868 --> 00:30:37,837
TO THE EDGE OF THE WORLD.

739
00:30:37,870 --> 00:30:41,340
- AND IF YOU WANT TO GO THERE--
- TAKE THE SANTA MONICA FREEWAY.

740
00:30:41,373 --> 00:30:45,478
...YOU MUST BUILD A BOAT WHICH
WILL CARRY YOU OVER THE WAVES
LIKE A WHITE SWAN.

741
00:30:45,512 --> 00:30:47,280
TELL US, VAINAMOINEN,

742
00:30:47,313 --> 00:30:49,715
HOW CAN WE BUILD A BOAT
SUCH AS THAT?

743
00:30:49,748 --> 00:30:53,118
I'M GLAD YOU ASKED.
I'M HAVING
A BOAT-BUILDING SEMINAR.

744
00:30:53,152 --> 00:30:55,888
IN THIS ANCIENT OAK TREE,
YOU WILL FIND YOUR BOAT.

745
00:30:55,922 --> 00:30:57,890
YOU HAVE BUT TO TAKE IT OUT,

746
00:30:57,923 --> 00:31:02,128
AND IT WILL CARRY YOU
ACROSS THE SEA
TO THE SHORES OF POHJOLA.

747
00:31:02,162 --> 00:31:05,030
OKAY, HOW MUCH IS THIS
GONNA SET ME BACK?

748
00:31:07,833 --> 00:31:11,003
OH, I'M CHAFIN' LIKE ME.

749
00:31:11,037 --> 00:31:13,640
[LAUGHS]
OOPS. I DID IT AGAIN.

750
00:31:13,673 --> 00:31:16,775
YOU KIDDING ME?
A BOAT IN HERE?

751
00:31:16,808 --> 00:31:19,445
IT'S A CHIP-AWAY GAME.

752
00:31:19,478 --> 00:31:22,215
IS THERE ANOTHER WISE MAN
WE COULD TALK TO?

753
00:31:22,248 --> 00:31:24,217
EIGHT YEARS LATER...
[CHUCKLING]

754
00:31:24,250 --> 00:31:27,987
SO, ANYWAY, THAT'S WHAT
REALLY GOT ME INTERESTED
IN STAMP COLLECTING.

755
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:29,688
OF COURSE,
I'VE ALWAYS LOVED THE THEATER.

756
00:31:29,722 --> 00:31:31,390
JUST SHUT UP.

757
00:31:33,292 --> 00:31:35,562
[MOCK GRUNTING]

758
00:31:35,595 --> 00:31:38,063
HEY, NO BOAT.

759
00:31:38,097 --> 00:31:41,267
THAT'S MY SCRATCHING TREE,
YOU JERKS.

760
00:31:43,168 --> 00:31:46,505
UH, NOT THAT TREE.

761
00:31:49,042 --> 00:31:52,145
- [SNICKERS]
- UH, FRED, DID I MENTION
THAT I HAVE A BOAT?

762
00:31:52,178 --> 00:31:54,680
- SORRY.
- NO.

763
00:31:54,713 --> 00:31:57,650
OH, NOW THEY'RE
JUST SHOWING OFF.

764
00:31:57,683 --> 00:32:00,320
OH, NOW, WHAT DID THEY
CHOP THE SAIL OUT OF?

765
00:32:00,353 --> 00:32:03,022
- OH, THEY CUT THE WOOD
REAL THIN. REALLY.
- UH-HUH.

766
00:32:03,055 --> 00:32:07,327
MAY THE SUN LIGHT THE WAY
TO BRING YOU SAFELY HOME AGAIN.

767
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:09,928
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH.
CAN THE BALLOON JUICE, GRAMPS.
WE'RE OUTTA HERE.

768
00:32:09,962 --> 00:32:14,000
HEY, SHOULDN'T WE PATCH
THE BOTTOM FIRST?

769
00:32:14,033 --> 00:32:16,668
I JUST PRAY THERE AREN'T
NO PORTAGES.

770
00:32:18,203 --> 00:32:22,675
- OH, BOY.
- THE STAY PUFT MARSHMALLOW MAN
IN CHAINS?

771
00:32:22,708 --> 00:32:24,610
KINKY.

772
00:32:24,643 --> 00:32:26,512
IT'S GIANT SWEETBREADS.

773
00:32:26,545 --> 00:32:29,582
IT'S BODY WARS.

774
00:32:29,615 --> 00:32:32,618
SOMEONE HAS COME TO VISIT US!

775
00:32:32,652 --> 00:32:35,688
QUICK, PICK UP THE PLACE,
MAKE YOURSELF PRESENTABLE!

776
00:32:35,722 --> 00:32:38,023
- [MALE VOICE] WHERE?
- [MALE VOICE #2] OVER HERE.

777
00:32:38,057 --> 00:32:41,660
- NEAR ME.
- WHAT, IT'S A BAG
OF HOMER SIMPSONS?

778
00:32:41,693 --> 00:32:43,697
- WHO ARE YOU?
- [FEMALE VOICE] WE ARE WINDS.

779
00:32:43,730 --> 00:32:45,365
WAIT. ONE AT A TIME, PLEASE.
COME ON.

780
00:32:45,398 --> 00:32:49,335
- --THE WIND?
- [FEMALE VOICE] YES.
I AM THE SOUTH WIND.

781
00:32:49,368 --> 00:32:51,570
DO YOU PROVIDE A SERVICE
OF SOME SORT?

782
00:32:51,603 --> 00:32:53,072
[MALE VOICE]
I AM THE WEST WIND.

783
00:32:53,105 --> 00:32:56,075
[MALE VOICE #2]
AND I-- I AM THE EAST WIND.

784
00:32:56,108 --> 00:33:00,347
PUT YOUR TEETH IN!
I CAN'T UNDERSTAND YOU!

785
00:33:00,380 --> 00:33:02,282
ARE YOU THE NORTH WIND?

786
00:33:02,315 --> 00:33:05,585
[MALE VOICE #3]
NO. I AM THE MIST.

787
00:33:05,618 --> 00:33:09,155
I'M RELATIVE HUMIDITY.
IT'S NOT SO MUCH THE HEAT
AS IT IS ME.

788
00:33:09,188 --> 00:33:12,325
♪ I'M THE SUMMER WIND
COME BLOWIN' IN ♪

789
00:33:12,358 --> 00:33:13,793
♪♪ [HUMMING]

790
00:33:15,995 --> 00:33:18,197
- AND YOU-- WHICH ONE ARE YOU?
- [MOCK CHUCKLING]

791
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:20,065
OH, ME?
I'M JUST THE LAUNDRY.

792
00:33:20,098 --> 00:33:22,235
[MALE VOICE #4]
I AM THE NORTH WIND.

793
00:33:22,268 --> 00:33:26,538
- CALL ME SANDY.
- I WAS BORN AMONG
THE ICE FLOES.

794
00:33:26,572 --> 00:33:29,775
OH, THAT'S FINE, THANK YOU.
[CHUCKLING]

795
00:33:29,808 --> 00:33:31,810
[NORTH WIND]
PLEASE LET ME OUT.

796
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,813
YEAH, I DIDN'T ASK
FOR A BIOGRAPHY.

797
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:37,283
VERY WELL.
I WILL LET YOU OUT.

798
00:33:37,317 --> 00:33:40,753
SO, THIS IS WHERE I FIND YOU,
MY LITTLE PET.

799
00:33:40,787 --> 00:33:42,755
UM, WE WEREN'T KISSING.
WE WERE JUST TALKING.

800
00:33:42,788 --> 00:33:45,692
PERHAPS YOU NEED
SOMETHING TO AMUSE YOU.

801
00:33:45,725 --> 00:33:49,395
JUST COME WITH ME.
I'LL FIND SOMETHING
FOR YOU TO DO.

802
00:33:49,428 --> 00:33:53,032
I'VE GOT ONE OF THOSE
LITTLE POOL TABLES
I BOUGHT AT BROOKSTONE.

803
00:33:53,065 --> 00:33:55,468
- YOU'LL LOVE IT.
- THROW MY PRISONER IN CHAINS!

804
00:33:55,502 --> 00:33:57,770
ALL RIGHT!
SOME ORDERS WE LIKE TO GET.
[CHUCKLING]

805
00:33:57,803 --> 00:34:00,372
- [SHOUTING]
- YEAH.

806
00:34:05,845 --> 00:34:08,380
DEEP THOUGHTS.

807
00:34:08,413 --> 00:34:10,483
OH, WALLEYE CHOP.

808
00:34:10,517 --> 00:34:12,685
I'D BETTER GET OUT THERE.

809
00:34:12,718 --> 00:34:14,987
ERIK'S SMALL CIGARS.

810
00:34:15,020 --> 00:34:17,523
INCONCEIVABLE.
THEY'RE GAINING ON US.

811
00:34:17,557 --> 00:34:21,693
- OH, THE KEG'S HERE.
- AH, HE'S COME,
AS I SAID HE WOULD.

812
00:34:21,727 --> 00:34:23,963
DO YOU SEE HIS BOAT
APPROACHING OUR SHORE?

813
00:34:23,997 --> 00:34:26,098
DO YOU HEAR THE WAVES
BRINGING HIM NEARER?

814
00:34:26,132 --> 00:34:28,968
COME. WAKE UP.
RUN TO THE BEACH
AND WELCOME HIM.

815
00:34:29,002 --> 00:34:32,037
YOU'RE THE BOSS.
YOU'RE THE QUEEN OF EVERYTHING.
OKAY.

816
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,973
SMILES, EVERYONE! SMILES!
[CHUCKLES]

817
00:34:35,007 --> 00:34:37,377
EH...

818
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:39,512
HEY, DO YOU HAVE A DOCK
OR SOMETHING?

819
00:34:39,545 --> 00:34:41,847
WE'D REALLY APPRECIATE IT!

820
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:43,515
[CHUCKLES]
LOOK AT THAT BOAT.

821
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:46,718
- WHAT, DID YOU CARVE IT
OUT OF A TREE?
- SHUT UP! SHUT UP!

822
00:34:46,752 --> 00:34:48,955
BOAT.

823
00:34:48,988 --> 00:34:51,190
MISTRESS, OH, YOU WERE RIGHT.

824
00:34:51,223 --> 00:34:52,892
THE BOAT
IS BRINGING LEMMINKAINEN--

825
00:34:52,925 --> 00:34:54,393
- MMM! [SMACKING LIPS]
- ...AND HIS FRIEND,

826
00:34:54,427 --> 00:34:57,163
THE IMMORTAL
BLACKSMITH ILLMARINEN.

827
00:34:57,197 --> 00:34:59,765
- GREETINGS FOR ALL!
- HI.

828
00:34:59,798 --> 00:35:01,900
WHO ACCEPTS THE CHALLENGE
THAT I HAVE BROUGHT?

829
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:04,103
- NOPE. CAN'T. GOT A BAD KNEE.
- I DID THE LAST CHALLENGE.

830
00:35:04,137 --> 00:35:06,338
I HAVE COME TO FREE
THE MAIDEN ANNIKKI.

831
00:35:06,372 --> 00:35:08,773
- I AM HERE WITH HER BROTHER.
- UH, TONY.

832
00:35:08,808 --> 00:35:11,643
- YOU ARE NO COWARD? THEN FIGHT!
- NOEL COWARD?

833
00:35:11,677 --> 00:35:14,713
IF YOUR POWER
CAN PROTECT YOU FROM MY ARROW.

834
00:35:14,747 --> 00:35:16,815
YES, MY POWER IS GREAT.

835
00:35:16,848 --> 00:35:19,685
UH, IT'S NOT THAT FUN
GOING TO GRANDMA'S ANYMORE.

836
00:35:19,718 --> 00:35:22,888
MAGIC AND CHARMS
AND TERRIBLE SPELLS--

837
00:35:22,922 --> 00:35:24,990
ENOUGH TO DRIVE YOU BACK
INTO THE BOILING HOME

838
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:27,260
FROM WHICH YOU COME,
YOU BLUNDERING FOOL.

839
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:29,628
THAT'S ENOUGH OF THAT.
YOU IMAGINE WE'VE COME HERE

840
00:35:29,662 --> 00:35:31,397
TO LISTEN TO
AN OLD WOMAN RAVING?

841
00:35:31,430 --> 00:35:33,967
- THAT'S WHY MOST PEOPLE COME.
- NOW, DO YOU ACCEPT
THE CHALLENGE,

842
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,935
OR WILL YOU GIVE UP
MY SISTER WITHOUT IT?

843
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:37,437
- TAKE THE CURTAIN.
- GO FOR THE BOX.

844
00:35:37,470 --> 00:35:39,605
I WILL NOT GIVE UP ANNIKKI.

845
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:41,840
- ...BUST THE WITCH'S BOSOM.
- NO, WAIT!

846
00:35:41,873 --> 00:35:43,375
- LET ME TAKE OFF MY GIRDLE.
- WAIT NOW!

847
00:35:43,408 --> 00:35:45,578
I WILL GIVE
YOUR MAIDEN BACK TO YOU

848
00:35:45,612 --> 00:35:48,380
IF YOU PERFORM
TWO SIMPLE TASKS FOR ME.

849
00:35:48,413 --> 00:35:50,817
- AW, THIS BITES. LET'S BLOW.
- WHAT ARE THEY?

850
00:35:50,850 --> 00:35:52,952
PICK UP MY DRY CLEANING
AND CALL THE VET.

851
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:55,253
I HAVE A FIELD
OVERRUN WITH SNAKES,

852
00:35:55,287 --> 00:35:57,690
AND HE MUST FIRST PLOW IT.

853
00:35:57,723 --> 00:36:00,760
- ALL RIGHT.
- IT'S WEIRD, BUT...

854
00:36:00,793 --> 00:36:02,895
- TELL ME WHERE YOUR FIELD IS.
- COME ON.

855
00:36:02,928 --> 00:36:06,265
COME ON, GOOD LEMMINKäINEN.

856
00:36:07,667 --> 00:36:09,635
DON'T WAIT UP, ERIK,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

857
00:36:09,668 --> 00:36:12,372
- SAY, THAT IS COLD.
- [LAUGHS]

858
00:36:15,207 --> 00:36:17,175
YOU SEE IT BEFORE YOU.

859
00:36:17,210 --> 00:36:19,312
I SEE AN EL GRECO.

860
00:36:19,345 --> 00:36:21,813
[LOUHI]
A FIELD OF SNAKES.

861
00:36:21,847 --> 00:36:23,715
HEY, KEVIN COSTNER'S
IN THAT, ISN'T HE?

862
00:36:23,748 --> 00:36:26,718
- NO, THIS IS THE DIRTY VERSION.
- OH.

863
00:36:26,752 --> 00:36:30,522
I WANT A PLOW, AND I MUST HAVE
A POWERFUL HORSE WITH IT.

864
00:36:30,557 --> 00:36:32,525
HEY,
I'M THE CURSE BOSS HERE.

865
00:36:32,558 --> 00:36:35,493
...TO FEED ONE OF MY HORSES
TO THOSE SNAKES?

866
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:38,197
NEEDS A HORSE.
I WILL BUILD HIM A HORSE.

867
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:40,232
I'LL MAKE IT OUT OF A TREE.

868
00:36:40,265 --> 00:36:42,167
UH--OH.

869
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,635
HORSE CHESTNUT.
[LAUGHS]

870
00:36:43,668 --> 00:36:44,637
OH, MISTRESS.

871
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:46,605
DON'T CALL ME THAT
IN PUBLIC.

872
00:36:48,373 --> 00:36:52,077
YOU MUST NOT ALLOW ILLMARINEN
TO BUILD THAT HORSE.

873
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:55,582
HE'LL BE SURE TO PLOW THE FIELD,
AND THEY WILL TAKE ANNIKKI.

874
00:36:55,615 --> 00:36:58,183
AND ILLMARINEN WILL REFUSE
TO MAKE US A SAMPO.

875
00:36:58,217 --> 00:36:59,718
HAVE PATIENCE.

876
00:36:59,752 --> 00:37:02,322
HE WON'T BE ABLE
TO CARRY HER AWAY.

877
00:37:02,355 --> 00:37:04,123
NOW, SLIP INTO THAT
STABLE BOY SUIT

878
00:37:04,157 --> 00:37:05,958
AND MEET ME LATER
DOWN BY THE [WHISPERS].

879
00:37:05,992 --> 00:37:09,295
[LAUGHS]
YES, MISTRESS. OH, MY.

880
00:37:11,963 --> 00:37:12,998
OOH. UH-OH.

881
00:37:13,032 --> 00:37:14,133
WOW.

882
00:37:14,167 --> 00:37:16,402
AND THE SCULLING CREW
TAKES TO THE LAKE.

883
00:37:16,435 --> 00:37:18,637
WE'VE GOT TO GET
ORGANIZED.

884
00:37:18,670 --> 00:37:22,308
ATTICA! ATTICA! ATTICA!

885
00:37:22,342 --> 00:37:24,410
IT'S THE OSLO RIOTS.

886
00:37:24,443 --> 00:37:27,112
HEY, UH, THAT'S NOT VERY SMART
WHEN YOU'RE IN THE BOAT.

887
00:37:27,145 --> 00:37:28,713
HE'S POUNDING
THE AIR THERE.

888
00:37:28,747 --> 00:37:29,715
IT'S AN AIR HAMMER.

889
00:37:29,748 --> 00:37:32,285
[LAUGHTER]

890
00:37:32,318 --> 00:37:34,587
HEY, WE'RE GOIN' OVER
TO SVEN'S AFTER, HUH?

891
00:37:34,620 --> 00:37:35,755
WANT TO?

892
00:37:36,822 --> 00:37:37,790
HUH?

893
00:37:37,823 --> 00:37:39,458
SUDDENLY IT'S FLASHDANCE.

894
00:37:39,492 --> 00:37:42,762
♪ HE'S A STEEL TOWN'S FAN
ON A SATURDAY NIGHT ♪

895
00:37:42,795 --> 00:37:45,430
WEIRD.

896
00:37:45,463 --> 00:37:47,032
OKAY. OKAY.

897
00:37:47,065 --> 00:37:50,402
IF HE CAN MAKE A HORSE,
WHY'D HE HAVE TO CUT
THAT TREE DOWN?

898
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:52,103
MM.

899
00:37:52,137 --> 00:37:53,838
YEAH, WELL,
NOW I JUST SIT BACK

900
00:37:53,872 --> 00:37:55,908
AND RAKE IN THE PRAISE,
PRETTY MUCH.

901
00:37:55,942 --> 00:37:58,243
HELLO, DADDY.
[LAUGHS]

902
00:37:58,277 --> 00:37:59,912
THE TRISTAR LOGO'S READY.

903
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:01,580
HE'S...

904
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:03,582
SAFE.

905
00:38:07,085 --> 00:38:10,188
♪ THEY RAN CALLIN'
WILDFIRE ♪

906
00:38:10,222 --> 00:38:12,692
♪ WHOO ♪

907
00:38:12,725 --> 00:38:16,362
OUCH. PHEW. STINGY.
THAT'S STILL HOT.

908
00:38:16,395 --> 00:38:18,697
HELLO.
I'M FROM THE TEMP AGENCY.

909
00:38:18,730 --> 00:38:21,100
I'M YOUR HORSE
FOR THE DAY.

910
00:38:22,402 --> 00:38:25,403
OH. SPEED THE PLOW.

911
00:38:25,437 --> 00:38:28,840
HEY, GOOD TIMING.
BOY, WE WORK GOOD TOGETHER.

912
00:38:28,873 --> 00:38:32,412
COULD YOU RUB SOME SOLARCAINE
ON ME, PLEASE?

913
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:36,548
A HORSE.
WE DIDN'T PLAN ON THAT.

914
00:38:36,582 --> 00:38:39,585
WOULD SOMEONE PLEASE
TURN THE WAGNER OFF?

915
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:42,455
HEY, I THINK HE JUST
INVENTED THE MOBIL LOGO.

916
00:38:42,488 --> 00:38:44,423
OH. NEAT.

917
00:38:46,792 --> 00:38:48,993
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

918
00:38:49,028 --> 00:38:50,628
EW.

919
00:38:50,662 --> 00:38:51,897
YECH.

920
00:38:51,930 --> 00:38:53,932
SNAKIES.

921
00:38:53,965 --> 00:38:56,202
IT'S KIND OF A GOOFY,
SCANDINAVIAN DOUBLE-DARE.

922
00:38:56,235 --> 00:38:58,170
[LAUGHS]

923
00:38:59,705 --> 00:39:01,273
OH, MAN.
IT'S A PUPPET. LOOK.

924
00:39:01,307 --> 00:39:02,842
HE'S BEING ATTACKED
BY A WOOZLE.

925
00:39:02,875 --> 00:39:04,310
[LAUGHS]

926
00:39:04,343 --> 00:39:06,978
YEAH, THEY'RE--THEY'RE ALL
YELLIN' "FAKE." HA!

927
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:09,848
AND NOW I'D LIKE TO DO MY
NASTASSJA KINSKI IMPRESSION.

928
00:39:09,882 --> 00:39:11,150
I'LL JUST TAKE
OFF MY CLOTHES.

929
00:39:11,183 --> 00:39:12,852
[LAUGHS]

930
00:39:12,885 --> 00:39:15,153
I KNEW THEY'D "WORM"
THEIR WAY INTO THE FILM.

931
00:39:15,187 --> 00:39:16,488
[LAUGHS]
WORM--

932
00:39:16,522 --> 00:39:18,257
SNAKES.

933
00:39:18,290 --> 00:39:21,393
YOU KNOW, I WONDER IF THAT HORSE
COMES IN ANY OTHER COLORS.

934
00:39:22,962 --> 00:39:25,230
UH, HE'S THE ENEMY,
BUT YOU GOTTA ADMIRE HIM.

935
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:26,932
YUP. YUP.
TIP YOUR CAP.

936
00:39:26,965 --> 00:39:28,767
UH, PRETTY MUCH.

937
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:31,170
GET A LOOK AT THIS,
HUH?

938
00:39:31,203 --> 00:39:33,905
NOW, LET'S GO IN AND SEE
IF MOM'S GOT DINNER READY.

939
00:39:36,075 --> 00:39:38,177
OH, GREAT.
WE CAN PLANT MORE SNAKES NOW.

940
00:39:38,210 --> 00:39:39,745
[LAUGHS]

941
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:43,382
ALL RIGHT.
I'VE FINISHED PLOWING
YOUR FIELD.

942
00:39:43,415 --> 00:39:44,650
PLANTED NOW WITH CARE.

943
00:39:44,683 --> 00:39:45,818
[GRUNTS]

944
00:39:45,852 --> 00:39:48,487
AND MAY THE GRAIN GROW
AS HIGH AS MY SHOULDER.

945
00:39:48,520 --> 00:39:49,655
NOW, WHERE IS SHE?

946
00:39:49,688 --> 00:39:52,023
WE WANT TO TAKE HER BACK.

947
00:39:52,057 --> 00:39:54,193
I'LL GIVE YOU
YOUR ANNIKKI.

948
00:39:54,227 --> 00:39:56,562
BUT IT WON'T
DO YOU MUCH GOOD.

949
00:39:56,595 --> 00:39:58,930
THERE ISN'T VERY MUCH LEFT
OF YOUR BOAT.

950
00:39:58,963 --> 00:40:00,767
D'OH--HEY.
THAT'S BELOW THE BELT.

951
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:02,535
YEAH, I DON'T REALLY GET
WITCHES' HUMOR.

952
00:40:02,568 --> 00:40:03,535
MM-MM.

953
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:06,672
COME ALONG.
LET ME SHOW YOU.

954
00:40:06,705 --> 00:40:08,340
BROTHER.
SHE'S GOT ISSUES, HUH?

955
00:40:08,373 --> 00:40:10,175
MM.

956
00:40:12,177 --> 00:40:14,213
IT'S THE SWEDISH DELLS.

957
00:40:14,247 --> 00:40:17,650
THE DUCKS. RIDE THE DUCKS.

958
00:40:17,683 --> 00:40:20,987
HEY. YOU WRECKED OUR BOAT
YOU FREAKED-OUT MANIAC.

959
00:40:22,353 --> 00:40:25,323
A GREAT FISH
WAS SWIMMING NEAR THE SHORE.

960
00:40:25,357 --> 00:40:26,492
UH-HUH.

961
00:40:26,525 --> 00:40:29,262
IT FLIPPED ITS TAIL ONCE
AND SMASHED YOUR BOAT.

962
00:40:29,295 --> 00:40:31,297
WELL I SUPPOSED THOSE
KIND OF THINGS HA--WHAT?

963
00:40:31,330 --> 00:40:33,898
...I WILL MAKE A NEW BOAT.
AN IRON ONE.

964
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:36,168
AND TELL YOUR FISH
IF HE TRIES TO SMASH THIS ONE

965
00:40:36,202 --> 00:40:37,503
IT'LL BREAK HIS TEETH OFF.

966
00:40:37,537 --> 00:40:39,772
WELL,
YOU DON'T HAVE TO YELL.

967
00:40:39,805 --> 00:40:42,273
HUH? WHAT?

968
00:40:42,307 --> 00:40:43,975
THEY'RE ROASTING
BULLWINKLE.

969
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:44,977
[GASPS]

970
00:40:45,010 --> 00:40:46,945
NO.

971
00:40:50,048 --> 00:40:51,950
SAVE ME, ROCKY.
HELP ME.

972
00:40:51,983 --> 00:40:53,885
AGAIN?

973
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:55,253
OH, NOBODY EVER HELPS
THIS GUY.

974
00:40:55,287 --> 00:40:57,523
LOOK! A BOAT!

975
00:40:58,857 --> 00:41:02,495
WUH-OH.
OUTTA CONTROL.

976
00:41:02,528 --> 00:41:04,263
[GASPS]

977
00:41:04,297 --> 00:41:05,932
WHAT'S GOING TO BECOME
OF US NOW?

978
00:41:05,965 --> 00:41:07,867
OH, EVERYTHING'S ABOUT YOU,
ISN'T IT?

979
00:41:07,900 --> 00:41:10,335
WHEN LOG FLUME RIDES
GO HORRIBLY WRONG.

980
00:41:10,368 --> 00:41:12,638
YOU MAY GET BURNT
ON THIS RIDE.

981
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:15,573
[SCREAMS]

982
00:41:15,607 --> 00:41:17,877
UH, THERE'S A FLAMING MOOSE
BLOCKING TRAFFIC

983
00:41:17,910 --> 00:41:19,478
ON I-35 W NORTHBOUND.

984
00:41:19,512 --> 00:41:20,778
WOULD SOMEBODY
PLEASE PUT ME OUT?

985
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,047
I SEEM TO BE ON FIRE.

986
00:41:23,748 --> 00:41:24,983
PROTECT US.

987
00:41:25,017 --> 00:41:26,752
HAVE MERCY, DEAR MISTRESS.
CHASE IT AWAY.

988
00:41:26,785 --> 00:41:28,587
DO SOMETHING.

989
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:30,655
NOW, THERE'S SOMETHING
YOU DON'T SEE EVERYDAY,
CHAUNCEY.

990
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:31,690
UH, WHAT'S THAT, EDGAR?

991
00:41:31,723 --> 00:41:33,225
KISS GOIN' BASS FISHIN'.

992
00:41:33,258 --> 00:41:34,293
HUH.

993
00:41:34,327 --> 00:41:35,693
QUITE A BOAT,
WOULDN'T YOU SAY?

994
00:41:35,727 --> 00:41:36,695
NOW THAT IT'S FINISHED,

995
00:41:36,728 --> 00:41:37,697
WE'LL BE ON OUR WAY

996
00:41:37,730 --> 00:41:38,797
THE MINUTE YOU
GIVE US ANNIKKI.

997
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:40,532
I DEMAND THAT YOU
MAKE YOUR BOAT STOP.

998
00:41:40,565 --> 00:41:42,200
WHEN YOU RELEASE MY SISTER.

999
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:44,168
YOUR ONLY EXCUSE BEFORE
WAS BECAUSE

1000
00:41:44,203 --> 00:41:45,403
YOUR FISH RAKED
OUR OTHER BOAT.

1001
00:41:45,437 --> 00:41:47,438
UGH, POINT WELL TAKEN.

1002
00:41:47,472 --> 00:41:50,108
YOU ACT LIKE
I'M THE BAD GUY.

1003
00:41:50,142 --> 00:41:52,510
I DON'T KNOW IF YOUR SISTER
IS READY FOR THAT.

1004
00:41:52,545 --> 00:41:54,012
SHE'S STILL
UPSTAIRS DRESSING.

1005
00:41:54,045 --> 00:41:56,148
...LADY OF POHJOLA.

1006
00:41:56,182 --> 00:41:58,950
YOU BETTER GIVE US ANNIKKI.

1007
00:41:58,983 --> 00:42:02,120
ONLY HE HAS PERFORMED WELL
WHAT I GAVE HIM TO DO.

1008
00:42:02,153 --> 00:42:03,822
AND YOU.
WHAT DID YOU DO?

1009
00:42:03,855 --> 00:42:04,823
YEAH.

1010
00:42:04,857 --> 00:42:07,593
I'VE HEARD YOU
MAKE MAGIC TOO.

1011
00:42:07,627 --> 00:42:08,727
HELL,
I MADE THE HORSE.

1012
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:09,728
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

1013
00:42:09,762 --> 00:42:11,863
WHAT MAGIC?

1014
00:42:11,897 --> 00:42:14,567
I MEAN,
THE SAMPO.

1015
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:17,002
♪ DUN DUN DUN ♪

1016
00:42:17,035 --> 00:42:19,137
YOU'LL FORGE A SAMPO.

1017
00:42:19,170 --> 00:42:21,640
OR YOU'LL NEVER SEE THE FACE
OF YOUR PRETTY SISTER AGAIN.

1018
00:42:21,673 --> 00:42:22,842
CAN WE SEE
THE OTHER PARTS?

1019
00:42:22,875 --> 00:42:24,843
UGH, CRIMINY.
BETTER LOOK UP "SAMPO" QUICK.

1020
00:42:24,877 --> 00:42:26,312
I THINK SHE'S SERIOUS.

1021
00:42:26,345 --> 00:42:29,382
ONLY A SAMPO.

1022
00:42:38,790 --> 00:42:40,960
NO, TOM. YOU'RE THINKING
OF A "SAMPLE."

1023
00:42:40,993 --> 00:42:43,962
S-A-M-P-L-E. WE'RE TALKING
ABOUT SAMPO WITH AN "O."

1024
00:42:43,995 --> 00:42:45,030
OH.

1025
00:42:45,063 --> 00:42:46,298
OKAY. OKAY. OKAY.
OKAY. OKAY. OKAY.

1026
00:42:46,332 --> 00:42:48,067
SO IF A SAMPO
ISN'T A SMALL TASTE

1027
00:42:48,100 --> 00:42:49,902
OF NO-FAT CHEESE
AT THE GROCERY STORE,

1028
00:42:49,935 --> 00:42:51,370
THEN WHAT,
I IMPLORE YOU, IS IT?

1029
00:42:51,403 --> 00:42:52,972
WELL, I WAS THINKING
THAT MAYBE A SAMPO

1030
00:42:53,005 --> 00:42:54,172
IS REALLY GOOD
CAN OPENER.

1031
00:42:54,205 --> 00:42:56,375
NO. I THINK IT'S
A STRAPLESS EVENING GOWN.

1032
00:42:56,408 --> 00:42:58,643
YOU THINK EVERYTHING
IS A STRAPLESS EVENING GOWN.

1033
00:42:58,677 --> 00:43:00,045
I JUST THINK
THEY'RE NEAT IS ALL.

1034
00:43:00,078 --> 00:43:01,047
WHAT DO YOU THINK,
JOEL?

1035
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:02,513
UH, I THINK
A SAMPO'S LIKE

1036
00:43:02,547 --> 00:43:04,950
A HAND-HAMMERED CONCH BELT
WITH TURQUOISE INLAYS,

1037
00:43:04,983 --> 00:43:07,853
USED TO ACCENTUATE
AN OVERSIZED BLOUSE?

1038
00:43:07,887 --> 00:43:10,155
I THINK IT'S THAT DENT
BETWEEN THE NOSE AND LIP.

1039
00:43:10,188 --> 00:43:12,925
WELL, WHATEVER IT IS, THAT WITCH
WANTS IT MORE THAN ANYTHING.

1040
00:43:12,958 --> 00:43:15,327
SO, IT MUST BE SOME SORT
OF WRINKLE CREAM.

1041
00:43:15,360 --> 00:43:16,362
OH, NO.
I GOT IT.

1042
00:43:16,395 --> 00:43:18,597
SAMPO--A PROGRESSIVE,
NEW CORPORATION

1043
00:43:18,630 --> 00:43:19,998
WITH AN EYE TOWARDS
THE FUTURE.

1044
00:43:20,032 --> 00:43:22,735
SAMPO IS A CORPORATION
FOR PEOPLE, BY PEOPLE.

1045
00:43:22,768 --> 00:43:24,437
I THINK IT INCREASES
CORN YIELDS.

1046
00:43:24,470 --> 00:43:26,972
I THINK IT'S A NASTY, LITTLE,
RUBBER NOVELTY ITEM.

1047
00:43:27,005 --> 00:43:27,973
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

1048
00:43:28,007 --> 00:43:29,375
WELL,
MAYBE IT'S NOT TANGIBLE.

1049
00:43:29,408 --> 00:43:32,243
I MEAN, MAYBE SAMPO IS FOUND
IN THE LAUGHTER OF CHILDREN,

1050
00:43:32,277 --> 00:43:33,912
OR IN THE ROAR
OF THE TIDE,

1051
00:43:33,945 --> 00:43:36,015
OR IN THE CAPACITY
TO LOVE AND BE LOVED.

1052
00:43:36,048 --> 00:43:37,182
NO, I KNOW.

1053
00:43:37,215 --> 00:43:39,452
I THINK SAMPO IS A NEW
HIGH-ENERGY PROP COMIC.

1054
00:43:39,485 --> 00:43:40,685
YOU KNOW, LIKE, "LADIES AND
GENTLEMEN,

1055
00:43:40,718 --> 00:43:42,087
"THE FUNNY BONE IS PROUD TO
PRESENT--

1056
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,588
FUNNY MAN, SAMPO."

1057
00:43:43,622 --> 00:43:45,323
WELL, ONE THING'S FOR SURE
GENTLEMEN--

1058
00:43:45,357 --> 00:43:46,592
THE U.S. OF A. STILL MAKES

1059
00:43:46,625 --> 00:43:48,427
THE BEST DAMN SAMPOS
ON THE MARKET,

1060
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:50,428
AND I MEAN NOBODY
IS GONNA CHANGE THAT.

1061
00:43:50,462 --> 00:43:51,430
I--I'VE GOT IT.

1062
00:43:51,463 --> 00:43:52,765
IT--IT'S FRESH.
IT'S SASSY.

1063
00:43:52,798 --> 00:43:53,832
IT'S FREE. IT'S ME.

1064
00:43:53,865 --> 00:43:54,967
IT'S AN EXCITING,
NEW FRAGRANCE

1065
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:56,635
BY PRINCE MATCHABELLI.
[LAUGHS]

1066
00:43:56,668 --> 00:43:58,503
UH, NO, UM...

1067
00:43:58,537 --> 00:44:00,072
WELL, TO BE HONEST,
EVERYBODY,

1068
00:44:00,105 --> 00:44:01,673
WE DON'T KNOW
WHAT A SAMPO IS.

1069
00:44:01,707 --> 00:44:02,675
NOT A CLUE.

1070
00:44:02,708 --> 00:44:04,175
IF YOU KNOW
WHAT A SAMPO IS,

1071
00:44:04,208 --> 00:44:05,977
WRITE IN ON A PIECE OF PAPER,
THROW IT AWAY

1072
00:44:06,012 --> 00:44:07,345
AND THEN
TRY NOT TO THINK ABOUT IT.

1073
00:44:07,378 --> 00:44:08,613
YOU'LL BE GLAD YOU DID.

1074
00:44:08,647 --> 00:44:09,915
SAMPO.

1075
00:44:09,948 --> 00:44:11,783
WHOA. OH, NO.
WE GOT MOVIE SIGN.

1076
00:44:11,817 --> 00:44:12,952
LET'S GO.

1077
00:44:20,492 --> 00:44:22,427
DING. SAMPO UP.

1078
00:44:24,062 --> 00:44:26,932
OH, GEEZ.
WHAT A DAY. UGH.

1079
00:44:26,965 --> 00:44:28,467
YOU KNOW, I REALLY ADMIRE
HOW YOU STOOD FIRM

1080
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:30,035
ON THE SAMPO ISSUE,
YOUR WITCHY-NESS.

1081
00:44:30,068 --> 00:44:32,037
YOU DIDN'T GIVE AN INCH
AND I REALLY ADMIRE
THAT QUALITY.

1082
00:44:32,070 --> 00:44:34,038
WE'D LIKE TO SHOW YOU, UH, HOW
WE MAXIMIZE WAREHOUSE,

1083
00:44:34,072 --> 00:44:35,440
UH, TO INCREASE
SAMPO SHIPMENTS.
[LAUGHS]

1084
00:44:35,473 --> 00:44:36,475
IT'S REALLY EXCITING.

1085
00:44:36,508 --> 00:44:37,575
I THINK YOU SHOULD
COME ALONG

1086
00:44:37,608 --> 00:44:38,810
AND TAKE A LOOK
AT WHAT WE'RE DOING.

1087
00:44:38,843 --> 00:44:39,945
WELL?

1088
00:44:39,978 --> 00:44:41,247
I MUST HAVE
A WISP OF LAMB'S WOOL,

1089
00:44:41,280 --> 00:44:42,715
A FEATHER FROM A SWAN,

1090
00:44:42,748 --> 00:44:43,748
AND A BARLEYCORN.

1091
00:44:43,782 --> 00:44:44,883
YA HEAR THIS GUY?

1092
00:44:44,917 --> 00:44:47,352
GET HIM THE SMALLEST
OF THE FLOCK.

1093
00:44:47,385 --> 00:44:48,353
AND A SWAN.

1094
00:44:48,387 --> 00:44:50,588
AND A WHOLE BUSHEL
OF BARLEY.

1095
00:44:50,622 --> 00:44:52,892
AND SOME MINI DOUGHNUTS.

1096
00:44:57,830 --> 00:45:01,633
UM, CAN WE GET MARRIED?
WE'RE IN LOVE.

1097
00:45:01,667 --> 00:45:04,937
NOBODY ASKED FOR A GOOSE.
YOU TAKE THAT RIGHT AWAY.

1098
00:45:07,338 --> 00:45:09,608
HMM?

1099
00:45:09,642 --> 00:45:11,577
OH, NOW SOMEBODY'S SWEATER'S
GONNA HAVE A BIG FLAW.

1100
00:45:16,482 --> 00:45:19,050
YOU PUT YOUR FEATHER
IN BEFORE THE WOOL?

1101
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:21,018
HMM.

1102
00:45:23,255 --> 00:45:26,525
WITH THIS WOOL
WILL I CLOTHE YOU.

1103
00:45:26,558 --> 00:45:29,762
WITH THESE TEETH
WILL YOU BITE ME.

1104
00:45:29,795 --> 00:45:31,763
WITH THIS BARLEY
WILL I NOURISH YOU.

1105
00:45:31,797 --> 00:45:33,965
OH. HE'S MAKING
CHEX PARTY MIX.

1106
00:45:33,998 --> 00:45:35,067
OH.

1107
00:45:35,100 --> 00:45:36,067
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN--

1108
00:45:36,102 --> 00:45:38,237
THE MAGIC
OF ULYSSES S. GRANT.

1109
00:45:38,270 --> 00:45:40,905
...DESIRED--THE SAMPO.

1110
00:45:40,938 --> 00:45:43,708
SAMPO.

1111
00:45:43,742 --> 00:45:45,077
SAMPO.

1112
00:45:45,110 --> 00:45:48,480
"SAMPO" MEANS "FLAVOR."

1113
00:45:48,513 --> 00:45:52,317
NOW GIVE ME THE FIRE
THAT BURNED IN THE CLOUDS.

1114
00:45:52,350 --> 00:45:53,352
HUH?

1115
00:45:53,385 --> 00:45:54,620
HOW DARE YOU.

1116
00:45:54,653 --> 00:45:55,787
DON'T MENTION THAT.

1117
00:45:55,820 --> 00:45:56,788
IT'S DIRTY.

1118
00:45:56,822 --> 00:45:58,557
YOU WANT THE SAMPO?

1119
00:45:58,590 --> 00:46:00,992
THAT IS THE ONLY FIRE
I CAN FORGE IT IN.

1120
00:46:01,025 --> 00:46:02,795
IT HAS TO BE
THE HEAVENLY FLAME.

1121
00:46:02,828 --> 00:46:04,195
IS IT HOT IN HERE?

1122
00:46:04,228 --> 00:46:05,997
I WONDER IF THIS
IS SOME TRICK

1123
00:46:06,030 --> 00:46:08,900
TO DEPRIVE ME
OF THE HEAVENLY FIRE.

1124
00:46:08,933 --> 00:46:10,402
[GRUNTS]

1125
00:46:10,435 --> 00:46:12,637
BUT WE WON'T HAVE MUCH USE
FOR THAT IF HE MAKES THE MILL.

1126
00:46:12,670 --> 00:46:13,738
GIVE HIM THE FIRE.

1127
00:46:13,772 --> 00:46:14,740
WE'LL BE ABLE TO HAVE

1128
00:46:14,773 --> 00:46:15,940
AS MUCH FLOUR AS WE WANT

1129
00:46:15,973 --> 00:46:17,008
WITHOUT GRAIN.

1130
00:46:17,042 --> 00:46:18,143
AND WE'LL BE ABLE
TO HAVE SALT.

1131
00:46:18,177 --> 00:46:20,412
AND WE WILL BE ABLE
TO MAKE SILVER AND GOLD.

1132
00:46:20,445 --> 00:46:22,982
OH, LET HIM HAVE IT.
OH, PLEASE.

1133
00:46:23,015 --> 00:46:24,817
MY SPIN DOCTORS.

1134
00:46:24,850 --> 00:46:27,585
GO AND FETCH THE HEAVENLY FLAME
FOR HIM THEN.

1135
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:29,722
BUT SOMEONE STAY HERE
TO ANSWER THE PHONES.

1136
00:46:29,755 --> 00:46:31,723
BOY, SHE'S REALLY BROKEN THROUGH
THE GLASS CEILING, HUH?

1137
00:46:31,757 --> 00:46:33,692
OH, YEAH.

1138
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:38,530
♪ DUM DUM DUM DUM DUM DUM
DUM DUM DUM DUM DUM ♪

1139
00:46:38,563 --> 00:46:40,598
♪ DUM DUM DUM
DUM DUM DUM ♪

1140
00:46:40,632 --> 00:46:43,268
UM, YESTERDAY'S SOUP.
WE'RE TRYING TO GET RID OF IT.

1141
00:46:43,302 --> 00:46:45,903
MM. KINDA LOOKS
LIKE CALIGULA IN HERE.

1142
00:46:45,937 --> 00:46:47,638
HOW WOULD YOU KNOW THAT?

1143
00:46:50,308 --> 00:46:52,610
THE SOUP HAS A ESCORT?

1144
00:46:52,643 --> 00:46:54,713
[LAUGHS]

1145
00:46:54,747 --> 00:46:56,682
GOOD SOUP.

1146
00:46:59,383 --> 00:47:01,387
[GRUNTS]

1147
00:47:01,420 --> 00:47:03,055
HERE. DITCH THIS
FLAMIN' SKULL FOR ME.

1148
00:47:03,088 --> 00:47:05,923
I DON'T KNOW HOW
THAT GOT IN THERE.

1149
00:47:05,957 --> 00:47:07,258
NICE WEIGHT.

1150
00:47:07,292 --> 00:47:09,227
MM-HMM.
REAL GOOD FLAME.

1151
00:47:09,260 --> 00:47:10,228
MM-HMM.

1152
00:47:10,262 --> 00:47:12,030
NICE.

1153
00:47:14,365 --> 00:47:15,667
PUT ALL YOUR
IDLE PEOPLE TO WORK.

1154
00:47:15,700 --> 00:47:16,735
I'LL NEED THERE HELP.

1155
00:47:16,768 --> 00:47:19,270
TELL THEM TO WORK
THE BELLOWS.

1156
00:47:19,303 --> 00:47:20,905
YOU HEARD WHAT HE SAID.

1157
00:47:20,938 --> 00:47:23,042
SAUL BELLOWS.
GET TO WORK.

1158
00:47:23,075 --> 00:47:24,075
NO, NO.

1159
00:47:24,108 --> 00:47:26,043
OH.
[LAUGHS]

1160
00:47:27,778 --> 00:47:30,615
IS IT SAMPO YET?

1161
00:47:30,648 --> 00:47:31,850
[GRUNTS]

1162
00:47:31,883 --> 00:47:34,820
NOW, BE CAREFUL.
THIS PLATE IS VERY HOT.

1163
00:47:41,092 --> 00:47:44,328
SO, HOW DOES THIS WORK?

1164
00:47:44,362 --> 00:47:48,433
HEY, LET ME KNOW
WHEN YOU NEED A BREAK.

1165
00:47:48,467 --> 00:47:51,937
MARK VII.
MARK VII.

1166
00:47:51,970 --> 00:47:54,940
MARK VII, DAMN IT.
OH, MARK VII. WHEW.

1167
00:47:54,973 --> 00:47:58,443
FREEDOM TROLLS.
WORKING FOR YOU.

1168
00:47:58,477 --> 00:48:02,948
WHERE'S A FRIGGIN' SAMPO...
[SCOFFS]

1169
00:48:02,982 --> 00:48:06,050
UH, STEVE, HONEY?
WHY DON'T YOU GO GET
DADDY A BEER.

1170
00:48:06,083 --> 00:48:08,787
YOU SAID YOU'D MAKE THE MILL.
WHERE IS IT?

1171
00:48:08,820 --> 00:48:10,588
YOUR MEN CAN'T
MAKE THE FIRE HOT ENOUGH.

1172
00:48:10,622 --> 00:48:13,592
SURE.
BLAME MY DEPARTMENT.

1173
00:48:13,625 --> 00:48:15,160
GET WORKING,
YOU SLACKARDS.

1174
00:48:15,193 --> 00:48:16,262
OOH.

1175
00:48:16,295 --> 00:48:18,763
PUMP THE BELLOWS.
MAKE THE FLAMES LEAP UP.

1176
00:48:18,797 --> 00:48:20,165
WE'RE DOING OUR BEST,
MISTRESS.

1177
00:48:20,198 --> 00:48:22,167
HE'S GOT
A COCKTAIL DRESS ON.

1178
00:48:29,140 --> 00:48:30,175
AH, IT'S NOT DONE.

1179
00:48:30,208 --> 00:48:32,543
MUST HAVE BEEN FROZEN
IN THE MIDDLE.

1180
00:48:34,245 --> 00:48:36,715
HE'S GOT
DELUSIONS OF GRANDEUR.

1181
00:48:36,748 --> 00:48:39,150
HEY, IT'S LIKE
URBAN COWBOY.

1182
00:48:39,183 --> 00:48:41,118
[LAUGHS]

1183
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:49,093
[SERVO GROANS]
BOY, HOW'S THAT BEER
COMING, STEVIE?

1184
00:48:49,127 --> 00:48:52,763
WORK HARDER!
GET THE SEED OUT!

1185
00:48:52,797 --> 00:48:56,402
- FASTER! FASTER!
- GET OFF, TODD, COME ON,
I'M SERIOUS!

1186
00:48:56,435 --> 00:48:59,738
THEY THINK I'M WORKING,
THAT'S THE BEAUTY PART.

1187
00:49:03,275 --> 00:49:05,843
OH, I HATE THIS
INFERNAL ROUTINE.

1188
00:49:05,877 --> 00:49:07,545
♪ BURN, BABY, BURN ♪

1189
00:49:07,578 --> 00:49:10,148
♪ DISCO INFERNO ♪

1190
00:49:13,752 --> 00:49:16,388
OH, THE GUY ON TOP
MUST BE THE SHOP STEWARD.

1191
00:49:16,422 --> 00:49:18,790
AH.

1192
00:49:18,823 --> 00:49:21,893
WILL SOMEONE PLEASE
GET THE PHONE?

1193
00:49:21,927 --> 00:49:24,128
KIDS COME RUNNING FOR
THE RICH TASTE OF SAMPO.

1194
00:49:24,162 --> 00:49:26,965
MM.

1195
00:49:26,998 --> 00:49:28,400
[ALL]
OW!

1196
00:49:28,433 --> 00:49:29,835
BE CAREFUL,
THAT'S NITRIC ACID.

1197
00:49:29,868 --> 00:49:32,270
WE DON'T HAVE VERY MUCH.

1198
00:49:34,638 --> 00:49:35,973
[ALL]
OW!

1199
00:49:36,007 --> 00:49:38,077
I HATE THIS
SCHOOL LUNCH PROGRAM.

1200
00:49:38,110 --> 00:49:40,645
WATER'S CONSIDERED
A VEGETABLE.

1201
00:49:40,678 --> 00:49:42,747
UGH, THIS IS WHY
I DON'T MAKE SAMPOS

1202
00:49:42,780 --> 00:49:45,750
- EXCEPT ON HOLIDAYS.
- HEY, CAN WE HELP?

1203
00:49:45,783 --> 00:49:47,518
UH, YOU CAN HELP
BY SETTING THE TABLE.

1204
00:49:47,552 --> 00:49:49,387
OH.

1205
00:49:49,420 --> 00:49:52,257
SORRY, SAMPO'S OFF.

1206
00:49:52,290 --> 00:49:53,525
SAMPO...

1207
00:49:53,558 --> 00:49:55,360
ASK FOR IT BY NAME.

1208
00:49:55,393 --> 00:49:58,330
- SAMPO.
- ASK FOR IT BY NAME.

1209
00:49:58,363 --> 00:50:00,065
YEAH. THAT'S A SAMPO, HUH?

1210
00:50:00,098 --> 00:50:02,067
SAMPO.

1211
00:50:02,100 --> 00:50:03,802
RAY NITSCHKE?

1212
00:50:03,835 --> 00:50:05,437
YOU GET WAFERS WITH IT!

1213
00:50:05,470 --> 00:50:07,572
NO, YOU DON'T GET
ANY WAFERS WITH IT!

1214
00:50:07,605 --> 00:50:10,342
- I SAID I WOULD.
- IT'S VERY IMPRESSIVE,

1215
00:50:10,375 --> 00:50:11,943
BUT HOW DO I KNOW IT WORKS?

1216
00:50:11,977 --> 00:50:13,745
WELL, YOU JUST PLUG IT
INTO THE WALL OUTLET

1217
00:50:13,778 --> 00:50:15,247
AND TURN IT ON.

1218
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:17,148
LET THERE BE GOLD

1219
00:50:17,182 --> 00:50:19,683
AND FLOUR!

1220
00:50:19,718 --> 00:50:20,952
AND SALT!

1221
00:50:20,985 --> 00:50:23,955
OF COURSE, I RECOMMEND
THE SERVICE CONTRACT.

1222
00:50:23,988 --> 00:50:26,725
[MEN MURMUR]

1223
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:30,028
STILL, I THINK IT WOULD

1224
00:50:30,062 --> 00:50:32,897
LOOK BETTER BY THE COUCH.

1225
00:50:32,930 --> 00:50:36,402
SORRY I DOUBTED YOUR SAMPO.

1226
00:50:36,435 --> 00:50:38,870
MM. [SMACKS LIPS]

1227
00:50:40,738 --> 00:50:42,273
BOY, I THOUGHT
THERE'D BE MORE PEOPLE

1228
00:50:42,307 --> 00:50:43,608
AROUND THE GOLD PART
OF THIS THING,

1229
00:50:43,642 --> 00:50:45,443
BUT THE LINE'S REALLY
NOT THAT LONG, YOU KNOW?

1230
00:50:45,477 --> 00:50:47,345
THIS IS WHAT IT WOULD'VE BEEN
LIKE IF PEROT WOULD'VE WON.

1231
00:50:47,378 --> 00:50:49,647
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1232
00:50:49,680 --> 00:50:51,148
OH, GREAT, ROCK SALT!

1233
00:50:51,182 --> 00:50:54,152
WE'LL NEVER SLIP
ON THE DRIVEWAY AGAIN.

1234
00:50:56,655 --> 00:50:58,590
MAKES YOU THINK,
DON'T IT, HONEY?

1235
00:50:58,623 --> 00:51:01,460
NICE TO SEE 'EM SO HAPPY.

1236
00:51:01,493 --> 00:51:03,295
GOLD.

1237
00:51:03,328 --> 00:51:04,695
UH, THE MANUAL'S IN THE BOX.

1238
00:51:04,728 --> 00:51:07,198
AND THE FIRST UPGRADE'S FREE.

1239
00:51:07,232 --> 00:51:09,067
NOW GIVE US BACK ANNIKKI.

1240
00:51:09,100 --> 00:51:10,835
- OH, SHE'S HOME ALREADY.
- ALL RIGHT.

1241
00:51:10,868 --> 00:51:14,138
I WILL GIVE YOUR PRETTY SISTER
BACK TO YOU NOW.

1242
00:51:14,172 --> 00:51:16,942
I MUST WARN YOU,
SHE'S AGED SOME.

1243
00:51:19,710 --> 00:51:23,382
WAIT, THAT'S
THE WRONG SISTER.

1244
00:51:23,415 --> 00:51:26,452
GRAB YOURSELF A HEAPING
HELPING OF SWEET ANNIKKI.

1245
00:51:26,485 --> 00:51:29,053
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1246
00:51:31,422 --> 00:51:33,725
- ANNIKKI.
- DO I KNOW YOU?

1247
00:51:33,758 --> 00:51:35,793
- LEMMINKAINEN.
- YOU'RE NOT AS CUTE

1248
00:51:35,827 --> 00:51:38,297
AS I REMEMBER.

1249
00:51:38,330 --> 00:51:41,700
♪ ON A CLEAR DAY... ♪

1250
00:51:44,502 --> 00:51:48,373
ANNIKKI.
MY LITTLE SISTER.

1251
00:51:48,407 --> 00:51:50,442
TAKE THAT CREATURE
AWAY FROM MY PALACE!

1252
00:51:50,475 --> 00:51:52,310
- OH, KILLJOY.
- AFTER WHAT SHE'S DONE

1253
00:51:52,343 --> 00:51:54,578
WITH ALL THOSE
NASTY FLOWERS.

1254
00:51:54,612 --> 00:51:55,847
COME ON.

1255
00:51:55,880 --> 00:51:57,782
DON'T WORRY, LADY,
WE'RE OUTTA HERE.

1256
00:51:57,815 --> 00:51:59,818
GAH.

1257
00:52:02,020 --> 00:52:04,255
WELL, HEY, MISSUS,
THE SAMPO STOPPED WORKING,

1258
00:52:04,288 --> 00:52:06,958
AND WE DIDN'T GET
THE SERVICE CONTRACT.

1259
00:52:06,992 --> 00:52:08,860
SMASH IT AND TAKE THEM AWAY.

1260
00:52:08,893 --> 00:52:11,062
AND I WANT THEM
ALL INVENTORIED, TOO!

1261
00:52:11,095 --> 00:52:12,830
I DON'T WANT THEM HERE--

1262
00:52:12,863 --> 00:52:16,300
MAN, I WONDER WHAT HER
MEYERS-BRIGGS TEST WAS LIKE.

1263
00:52:16,333 --> 00:52:17,868
HOW WERE YOU EVER ABLE
TO RESCUE ME

1264
00:52:17,902 --> 00:52:19,737
- FROM THAT WICKED CREATURE?
- WELL, I HAD TO MAKE

1265
00:52:19,770 --> 00:52:21,005
THIS BOAT ALL BY MYSELF.

1266
00:52:21,038 --> 00:52:22,273
HEY, LEAVE MY SISTER ALONE.

1267
00:52:22,307 --> 00:52:23,942
YOUR BROTHER, ILLMARINEN,

1268
00:52:23,975 --> 00:52:25,810
MADE A SAMPO

1269
00:52:25,843 --> 00:52:27,312
AND LEFT IT WITH
THE WICKED WITCH

1270
00:52:27,345 --> 00:52:30,548
- IN PLACE OF YOU.
- A SAMPO?

1271
00:52:30,582 --> 00:52:32,083
YOU MEAN, ONE OF THOSE
BIG THINGS THAT MAKES

1272
00:52:32,117 --> 00:52:35,020
- GOLD AND SALTA AND STUFF?
- YEAH.

1273
00:52:36,487 --> 00:52:38,790
YOU MEAN THE NEW '92 SAMPO
WITH THE LEATHER INTERIOR?

1274
00:52:38,823 --> 00:52:40,125
IT'S BECAUSE OF ME.

1275
00:52:40,158 --> 00:52:42,960
HE DEPRIVED OUR PEOPLE
OF THEIR RIGHTFUL TREASURE.

1276
00:52:42,993 --> 00:52:45,297
I AM RETURNING TO POHJOLA,

1277
00:52:45,330 --> 00:52:47,898
AND I SHALL
RECOVER THE SAMPO.

1278
00:52:47,932 --> 00:52:49,333
NO, ILLMARINEN.

1279
00:52:49,367 --> 00:52:51,102
I AM GOING BACK FOR IT NOW.

1280
00:52:51,135 --> 00:52:52,837
OH, WELL, I THINK
A BETTER PLAN

1281
00:52:52,870 --> 00:52:54,105
WOULD BE TO GO BACK
AND GET SUPPLIES--

1282
00:52:54,138 --> 00:52:56,340
- HEY!
- HEY, HE'S GOT PURE WOOL ON!

1283
00:52:56,373 --> 00:52:58,710
HE'S GONNA SHRINK RIGHT UP!

1284
00:53:00,878 --> 00:53:03,248
TRY THE CLEANING POWER
OF NEW LEMON-KAINNEN

1285
00:53:03,282 --> 00:53:06,083
IN YOUR RINSE CYCLE.

1286
00:53:09,287 --> 00:53:10,822
THIS IS IT, ISN'T IT?

1287
00:53:10,855 --> 00:53:14,458
UH-HUH. I THINK SO.

1288
00:53:14,492 --> 00:53:16,460
UGH, REALLY LOVE
THE NEW SAMPO.

1289
00:53:16,493 --> 00:53:18,497
NO BUYER'S REMORSE HERE,
WITCHIE-POO.

1290
00:53:18,530 --> 00:53:21,700
WHO'S HUNGRY FOR SALT?

1291
00:53:21,733 --> 00:53:23,502
OH, JEEZ,
I'D BETTER PLAN THIS.

1292
00:53:23,535 --> 00:53:24,802
LET'S SEE. [CLEARS THROAT]

1293
00:53:24,835 --> 00:53:26,437
UH, GOTTA TAKE THE SAMPO.
IT'S MY DAD'S.

1294
00:53:26,470 --> 00:53:28,240
NO, NO, DAMN.
SAMPO REPAIR.

1295
00:53:28,273 --> 00:53:31,208
NO, NO, MIGHT I JUST POP IN
AND GRAB MY SAMPO?

1296
00:53:31,242 --> 00:53:34,012
NO! DARN. UGH.

1297
00:53:34,045 --> 00:53:35,747
OH, NO, THEY REALLY LIKE IT.

1298
00:53:35,780 --> 00:53:37,615
I WAS HOPING THEY WOULDN'T BE
GETTING INTO THE SAMPO.

1299
00:53:37,648 --> 00:53:39,417
NO SUCH LUCK.

1300
00:53:39,450 --> 00:53:41,218
MM, A GOOD HEFT.

1301
00:53:41,252 --> 00:53:42,853
I CAUGHT YOU,
YOU FILTHY WRETCH,

1302
00:53:42,887 --> 00:53:44,522
TRYING TO STEAL MY GOLD!

1303
00:53:44,555 --> 00:53:46,357
- I WASN'T!
- CATCH HIM!

1304
00:53:46,390 --> 00:53:48,158
DON'T LET HIM GET AWAY!

1305
00:53:48,192 --> 00:53:50,995
FIND HIM AND THROW HIM
INTO THE--

1306
00:53:51,028 --> 00:53:54,432
HEY, TONY, COME ON, IT'S ME!
YOUR ROOMMATE!

1307
00:53:54,465 --> 00:53:57,735
- MONKEY-PILE.
- OOH.

1308
00:53:57,768 --> 00:54:01,138
- PEW! UGH,
THAT WAS A MISTAKE.
- [JOEL COUGHS]

1309
00:54:01,172 --> 00:54:03,007
THAT WAS
THE CHILI RELLENO WIND.

1310
00:54:03,040 --> 00:54:04,675
EW!

1311
00:54:04,708 --> 00:54:06,110
OOH, OUCH.

1312
00:54:06,143 --> 00:54:08,045
WHO LET THE MIST OUT?

1313
00:54:08,078 --> 00:54:09,847
IT BLINDS ME
SO I CANNOT SEE.

1314
00:54:09,880 --> 00:54:11,783
- [SERVO COUGHS]
- BACK INTO MY BAG

1315
00:54:11,817 --> 00:54:14,552
MIST, COME BACK TO ME.
BACK INTO THY BAG.

1316
00:54:14,585 --> 00:54:16,487
WHY DID THEE
EVEN HAVE THE MIST

1317
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:18,657
IF IT BUGS THEE SO MUCH?

1318
00:54:18,690 --> 00:54:20,992
IT'S KIND OF LIKE A GIANT
NEOSYNEPHRINE BAG.

1319
00:54:21,025 --> 00:54:24,828
- ISN'T IT?
- [MEN MUTTER]

1320
00:54:24,862 --> 00:54:27,298
GONE!

1321
00:54:27,332 --> 00:54:29,233
MA'AM?

1322
00:54:29,267 --> 00:54:32,403
WHERE IS THE MANY-COLORED
DOME OF THE SAMPO?

1323
00:54:32,437 --> 00:54:35,240
MA'AM, THE DOME IS AN OPTION
THAT YOU DID NOT ORDER.

1324
00:54:35,273 --> 00:54:37,308
GO AFTER HIM
AND BRING HIM BACK HERE!

1325
00:54:37,342 --> 00:54:40,945
I CAN NEVER JUST SIT BACK
AND ENJOY MY SAMPO.

1326
00:54:40,978 --> 00:54:43,848
[MEN STRAIN]

1327
00:54:47,118 --> 00:54:50,022
HEY! IT'S NICE OUT HERE.

1328
00:54:52,290 --> 00:54:54,592
AH, THERE HE IS.

1329
00:54:54,625 --> 00:54:56,728
MISS AMERICA!

1330
00:54:56,762 --> 00:54:58,963
DESTROY LEMMINKAINEN'S BOAT!
RELEASE THEM!

1331
00:54:58,997 --> 00:55:02,667
LET THE WINDS RUSH FORTH
TO DESTROY THIS THIEF.

1332
00:55:02,700 --> 00:55:04,535
FLY, MONKEYS! FLY!

1333
00:55:04,568 --> 00:55:08,038
[CROW CACKLES]

1334
00:55:08,072 --> 00:55:10,275
OH, NOW WHY DOES THIS HAPPEN

1335
00:55:10,308 --> 00:55:12,743
AT 4:30 ON A FRIDAY?

1336
00:55:12,777 --> 00:55:14,612
- GAH.
- ♪ LEMMINKAINEN BOAT ♪

1337
00:55:14,645 --> 00:55:17,182
♪ EXCITING AND NEW ♪

1338
00:55:18,950 --> 00:55:21,452
AGUIRRE, THE WRATH OF GOD.

1339
00:55:24,355 --> 00:55:25,757
I'M GONNA GET
A BIGGER BOAT, RIGHT?

1340
00:55:25,790 --> 00:55:29,493
YEAH, WE'RE GONNA GET
A BIGGER BOAT, DEFINITELY.

1341
00:55:29,527 --> 00:55:30,895
MAKE THE WITCH A SAMPO.

1342
00:55:30,928 --> 00:55:34,632
WHAT THE HECK
WAS I THINKING, ANYWAY?

1343
00:55:34,665 --> 00:55:37,102
WIND, WITH MATTHEW MODINE
AND JENNIFER GREY.

1344
00:55:37,135 --> 00:55:40,905
NOW ON VIDEO.

1345
00:55:40,938 --> 00:55:43,040
HEY, IT LOOKS JUST LIKE
THE STATUE OF IWO JIMA,

1346
00:55:43,073 --> 00:55:44,942
IF YOU CROSS YOUR EYES AND GET
THE POLES WITH THOSE GUYS--

1347
00:55:44,975 --> 00:55:47,812
WELL.

1348
00:55:47,845 --> 00:55:50,782
HOLD ON, BUCK! HOLD ONTO
THE BOAT, BUCKY!

1349
00:55:50,815 --> 00:55:52,383
ANYBODY GOT ANY DRAMAMINE?

1350
00:55:52,417 --> 00:55:54,152
- NO.
- [CROW RETCHES]

1351
00:55:54,185 --> 00:55:57,155
