01:06:04,595 --> 01:06:06,597
OKAY.
OH, THAT'S FOR FUN.

1584
01:06:06,630 --> 01:06:09,500
UH, ARE YOU WITH THE BRIDE
OR THE FAILURE?

1585
01:06:12,068 --> 01:06:13,837
HUH. CHECK OUT THIS GUY.
HE LOOKS LIKE SOMETHING

1586
01:06:13,870 --> 01:06:15,538
YOU'D BUY IN A GIFT SHOP
UP NORTH.

1587
01:06:15,572 --> 01:06:16,973
[CHUCKLES]

1588
01:06:17,007 --> 01:06:20,177
NOW WHY'S HE WEARING
A HERSHEY'S KISS ON HIS HEAD?

1589
01:06:20,210 --> 01:06:21,878
HEY. IS THAT--?

1590
01:06:21,912 --> 01:06:23,313
- BRANDO'S HERE.
- IT'S BRANDO!

1591
01:06:23,347 --> 01:06:24,315
HEY, IT'S BRANDO!

1592
01:06:24,348 --> 01:06:28,118
HI, MR. BRANDO.

1593
01:06:28,152 --> 01:06:32,757
ALL RISE.
SANTA IS ENTERING THE LODGE.

1594
01:06:32,790 --> 01:06:34,425
WHAT THE HELL
IS GOING ON IN HERE?

1595
01:06:34,458 --> 01:06:37,060
THIS IS MY ROOM.

1596
01:06:40,497 --> 01:06:42,867
UH, JUST THROW THIS
ON THE GIFT TABLE, WOULD YOU?

1597
01:06:42,900 --> 01:06:45,102
DIDN'T HAVE TIME
TO WRAP IT.

1598
01:06:45,135 --> 01:06:48,605
HERE YOU GO.

1599
01:06:48,638 --> 01:06:51,908
THEY NEVER INVITE ME
TO ANYTHING!

1600
01:06:54,478 --> 01:06:57,280
MAY HEALTH AND HAPPINESS
BE WITH YOU

1601
01:06:57,313 --> 01:06:58,915
ALL THE DAYS OF YOUR LIFE.

1602
01:06:58,948 --> 01:07:01,785
- OH, NO.
- HE'S DRUNK.

1603
01:07:01,818 --> 01:07:04,655
HEALTH BE WITH YOU,
VAINAMOINEN.

1604
01:07:04,688 --> 01:07:08,625
YOU ARE KIND TO PAY A VISIT
TO OUR HUMBLE LITTLE COTTAGE.

1605
01:07:08,658 --> 01:07:10,093
OH, THANKS.

1606
01:07:10,127 --> 01:07:13,297
I SEE THIS COMING IN REAL HANDY.

1607
01:07:13,330 --> 01:07:15,398
[LAUGHS]
WHAT AM I? I'M A MOOSE.

1608
01:07:15,432 --> 01:07:17,502
GRANDPA,
THAT'S AUNT ESSY'S URN!

1609
01:07:17,535 --> 01:07:19,870
[IMITATES SPITTING, COUGHING]

1610
01:07:19,903 --> 01:07:23,273
YOUR BEER IS ALMOST TOO STRONG
FOR AN OLD MAN LIKE ME.

1611
01:07:23,307 --> 01:07:25,042
UGH. CORONARY. UGH.

1612
01:07:25,075 --> 01:07:26,743
IT'S THE JOLLY TROLL.

1613
01:07:26,777 --> 01:07:28,478
HMM?

1614
01:07:28,512 --> 01:07:33,117
OH, SHE'S CALLING
THE BATMAN.

1615
01:07:33,150 --> 01:07:35,718
HMM. MAYBE SHE'S MAD
'CAUSE SHE USED TO DATE
LEMMINKAINEN, AND...

1616
01:07:35,753 --> 01:07:36,853
YEAH, SHE'S LOTS OF LAUGHS,

1617
01:07:36,887 --> 01:07:38,422
BUT NOT THE KIND
YOU'D SETTLE DOWN WITH.

1618
01:07:38,455 --> 01:07:42,092
SHE'S FINE FOR JUNIOR YEAR,
BUT YOU GOTTA MOVE ON.

1619
01:07:42,125 --> 01:07:43,293
OOH.

1620
01:07:43,327 --> 01:07:44,895
[CHILD SCREAMS]

1621
01:07:44,928 --> 01:07:46,130
♪ THAT WAS THE NIGHT ♪

1622
01:07:46,163 --> 01:07:50,700
♪ THAT THE LIGHTS
WENT OUT IN FINLAND ♪

1623
01:07:50,733 --> 01:07:52,437
- [EVIL LAUGHTER]
- OH, LOOKS LIKE SHE'S

1624
01:07:52,470 --> 01:07:56,173
DRAGGING A MUFFLER THERE.

1625
01:07:56,207 --> 01:07:58,575
EVIL TIMES HAVE FALLEN

1626
01:07:58,608 --> 01:08:00,677
ON HAPPY KALEVALA.

1627
01:08:00,710 --> 01:08:03,613
COME ON. IT'S JUST
A CIRCUIT BREAKER, GRANDPA.

1628
01:08:03,647 --> 01:08:06,817
SHE'S STOLEN THE SUN.

1629
01:08:06,850 --> 01:08:09,153
GOLLY, HE'S REALLY CALM
IN A CRISIS.

1630
01:08:09,187 --> 01:08:11,022
HI.
SORRY ABOUT THE FAILURE.

1631
01:08:11,055 --> 01:08:13,757
FAIR WELL, GOOD FRIEND.

1632
01:08:13,790 --> 01:08:15,492
FAIR THE WELL,
KIND MISTRESS.

1633
01:08:15,525 --> 01:08:17,093
FAIR THE WELL.
THANK YOU.

1634
01:08:17,127 --> 01:08:19,997
UH, I HAD THE CUT-CRYSTAL BOWL
THAT THE DIP WAS IN.

1635
01:08:20,030 --> 01:08:24,100
UH, WELL, WE'LL COME BACK.

1636
01:08:24,135 --> 01:08:25,502
[SCOFFS]
GREAT WEDDING.

1637
01:08:25,535 --> 01:08:29,038
GET HALF A BUZZ ON, AND THEN
SENT HOME WITH A TORCH.

1638
01:08:29,072 --> 01:08:33,077
THERE CAN BE NO HAPPINESS
WITHOUT THE SUN.

1639
01:08:33,110 --> 01:08:36,780
OH, COME ON, KIRSTEN.
I'M A NIGHT PERSON. I LOVE IT.

1640
01:08:36,813 --> 01:08:39,150
KEEP FOR ME MY KANTALE.

1641
01:08:39,183 --> 01:08:40,350
TAKE A HIT IF YOU WANT TO.

1642
01:08:40,383 --> 01:08:42,787
NOW IT CAN ONLY REMAIN SILENT.

1643
01:08:42,820 --> 01:08:45,455
I MUST NOT PLAY ON IT

1644
01:08:45,488 --> 01:08:47,858
UNLESS THE SUN IS UP.

1645
01:08:47,892 --> 01:08:49,560
OH, MR. PARTICULAR.

1646
01:08:49,593 --> 01:08:50,895
EVERYTHING'S
GOTTA BE JUST RIGHT.

1647
01:08:50,928 --> 01:08:52,262
YEAH, LOOKS LIKE
THEY'RE TRYING

1648
01:08:52,295 --> 01:08:53,597
TO TAKE BACK THE NIGHT
OVER THERE.

1649
01:08:53,630 --> 01:08:56,300
- OH, I THINK
IT'S A MELANIE CONCERT.
- OH.

1650
01:09:07,110 --> 01:09:08,745
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

1651
01:09:08,778 --> 01:09:10,915
PRESENTING,
IN HER ONE-WOMAN SHOW,

1652
01:09:10,948 --> 01:09:11,915
GYPSY.

1653
01:09:11,948 --> 01:09:12,917
HERE WE GO.

1654
01:09:12,950 --> 01:09:15,552
- SHH.
- OH, SORRY.

1655
01:09:15,585 --> 01:09:19,055
♪ THERE'S A BIG FRONTIER
OUT THERE CALLED LIFE ♪

1656
01:09:19,088 --> 01:09:20,858
♪ I AIN'T NOBODY'S DAUGHTER ♪

1657
01:09:20,892 --> 01:09:22,793
♪ I AIN'T NOBODY'S WIFE ♪

1658
01:09:22,827 --> 01:09:26,163
♪ I'M GONNA STAKE
MY VERY OWN CLAIM OF LAND ♪

1659
01:09:26,197 --> 01:09:29,500
♪ AND YOU'RE GONNA
WANNA KNOW WHO I AM ♪

1660
01:09:29,533 --> 01:09:31,668
♪ I'M GYPSY ♪

1661
01:09:31,702 --> 01:09:33,570
♪ GYPSY ROSE ME ♪

1662
01:09:33,603 --> 01:09:36,607
♪ GYPSY ROSE NOT YOU ♪

1663
01:09:36,640 --> 01:09:38,142
♪ NOT YOU ♪

1664
01:09:38,175 --> 01:09:40,510
♪ OR YOU ♪

1665
01:09:40,543 --> 01:09:44,147
♪ GYPSY ROSE ♪

1666
01:09:44,180 --> 01:09:46,883
♪ ME ♪

1667
01:09:46,917 --> 01:09:49,620
♪ YAY ♪

1668
01:09:49,653 --> 01:09:50,620
ALL RIGHT.

1669
01:09:50,653 --> 01:09:51,622
GYPSY, YAY!

1670
01:09:51,655 --> 01:09:52,723
[APPLAUSE]

1671
01:09:52,757 --> 01:09:54,758
OH, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1672
01:09:54,792 --> 01:09:56,960
YOU KNOW,
WE'RE ALL TRAVELING.

1673
01:09:56,993 --> 01:10:01,232
YOU, ME, THAT LITTLE GOLD GUY
OVER THERE.

1674
01:10:01,265 --> 01:10:03,267
WE'RE TRAVELING
ON THE BIG TRIP OF LIFE,

1675
01:10:03,300 --> 01:10:05,268
AND SOMETIMES IT TURNS OUT

1676
01:10:05,302 --> 01:10:07,337
WE HAVEN'T PACKED
THE RIGHT CLOTHES

1677
01:10:07,370 --> 01:10:11,042
FOR OUR OWN PERSONAL JOURNEY.

1678
01:10:11,075 --> 01:10:12,610
OH.

1679
01:10:12,643 --> 01:10:15,545
I'VE BEEN STRUGGLING
TO MAKE ENDS MEET.

1680
01:10:15,578 --> 01:10:19,182
THE SOCIAL WORKER
STOPPED BY TODAY.

1681
01:10:19,215 --> 01:10:22,252
WE'LL GET BY. SOMEHOW.

1682
01:10:22,285 --> 01:10:25,255
THANK YOU!
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1683
01:10:25,288 --> 01:10:27,692
SO MOVING.

1684
01:10:27,725 --> 01:10:30,260
I'M SICK OF FIGHTING WITH YOU,
BOYFRIEND.

1685
01:10:30,293 --> 01:10:33,097
BUT I'M NOT GOING
TO WALK OUT THAT DOOR.

1686
01:10:33,130 --> 01:10:36,667
NO, SIR.
I'M GOING TO RUN OUT THAT DOOR.

1687
01:10:36,700 --> 01:10:39,035
- [APPLAUSE]
- THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1688
01:10:39,068 --> 01:10:41,038
- SHE'S A SURVIVOR.
- YEAH, YOU BET.

1689
01:10:41,072 --> 01:10:42,438
YOU KNOW,
I'VE SEEN HER BEFORE.

1690
01:10:42,472 --> 01:10:45,708
HEY, IS MY ACT INTERFERING
WITH YOUR CONVERSATION, BUDDY?

1691
01:10:45,742 --> 01:10:46,710
[LAUGHTER]

1692
01:10:46,743 --> 01:10:48,745
OKAY,
THREE GUYS TOGETHER, HUH?

1693
01:10:48,778 --> 01:10:51,282
WHAT? SOME SORT OF
LOVE CONNECTION SCREW UP?

1694
01:10:51,315 --> 01:10:52,683
[LAUGHTER]

1695
01:10:52,717 --> 01:10:55,352
THANK YOU.
OH, THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

1696
01:10:55,385 --> 01:10:56,987
WHAT A NIGHT, EVERYBODY.

1697
01:10:57,020 --> 01:11:00,390
BUT BEFORE I GO, I WANNA
TELL YOU A LITTLE STORY.

1698
01:11:00,423 --> 01:11:02,693
A STORY ABOUT A GAL...

1699
01:11:02,727 --> 01:11:03,927
WHO RAN THE HIGHER FUNCTIONS

1700
01:11:03,960 --> 01:11:05,828
OF A LITTLE SATELLITE
IN A SYNCHRONOUS ORBIT.

1701
01:11:05,862 --> 01:11:10,300
A GAL THAT EVERYONE THOUGHT
WAS PERHAPS A LITTLE SLOW,

1702
01:11:10,333 --> 01:11:14,405
A LITTLE NAIVE,
A LITTLE SIMPLE.

1703
01:11:14,438 --> 01:11:17,107
BUT LET ME TELL YOU SOMETHING
ABOUT THAT GAL.

1704
01:11:17,140 --> 01:11:20,110
SHE HAD SPIRIT,
SHE HAD GUTS,

1705
01:11:20,143 --> 01:11:23,180
AND MOST OF ALL,
SHE HAD A HUGE HEART.

1706
01:11:23,213 --> 01:11:25,015
THAT GAL WAS ON HER JOURNEY,

1707
01:11:25,048 --> 01:11:27,417
AND WHEN HER LUGGAGE ENDED UP
ON ANOTHER PLANET,

1708
01:11:27,450 --> 01:11:29,353
THAT GAL PICKED HERSELF UP,

1709
01:11:29,387 --> 01:11:30,853
DUSTED HERSELF OFF,

1710
01:11:30,887 --> 01:11:34,692
AND WORE THE SAME OUTFIT
TWO DAYS IN A ROW.

1711
01:11:34,725 --> 01:11:37,227
THAT PLUCKY LITTLE GAL

1712
01:11:37,260 --> 01:11:40,297
IS ME.

1713
01:11:40,330 --> 01:11:42,198
OH, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1714
01:11:42,232 --> 01:11:43,200
[APPLAUSE]\

1715
01:11:43,233 --> 01:11:44,200
OH, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1716
01:11:44,233 --> 01:11:45,868
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1717
01:11:45,902 --> 01:11:47,170
WE'VE GOT COMMERCIAL SIGN.

1718
01:11:47,203 --> 01:11:49,238
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
I'M DON AMECHE.

1719
01:11:49,272 --> 01:11:51,075
I'LL BE HERE ALL WEEK.
THANK YOU.

1720
01:11:58,582 --> 01:12:01,585
HEY, LOOK! IT'S SKYLAB.

1721
01:12:01,618 --> 01:12:04,955
- [WHISTLING]
- [SERVO WHISTLES]

1722
01:12:04,988 --> 01:12:07,725
HEY, MOMMY'S BACK,
AND I'VE GOT PRESENTS!

1723
01:12:07,758 --> 01:12:09,560
NOW, OPEN THE BAG

1724
01:12:09,593 --> 01:12:12,162
AND RELEASE THE BLIZZARD!

1725
01:12:12,195 --> 01:12:14,197
MAY THE NORTH WIND
BRING SNOW

1726
01:12:14,230 --> 01:12:17,100
TO BLANKET THE LAND
OF KALEVALA

1727
01:12:17,133 --> 01:12:18,668
FOREVER!

1728
01:12:18,702 --> 01:12:22,505
AND MAY YOU STAY
FOREVER, YAH!

1729
01:12:22,538 --> 01:12:25,908
MEANWHILE, IN FROSTBITE FALLS,
MINNESOTA.

1730
01:12:25,942 --> 01:12:27,377
WE HAVE SOME
SCHOOL CLOSINGS TODAY,

1731
01:12:27,410 --> 01:12:29,178
INCLUDING STOCKHOLM,
PUBLIC AND PRIVATE.

1732
01:12:29,212 --> 01:12:30,580
OSLO, PUBLIC AND PAROCHIAL.

1733
01:12:30,613 --> 01:12:34,183
HELSINKI VO-TECH,
SUOMI JUNIOR HIGH.

1734
01:12:34,217 --> 01:12:36,353
- BOY, THAT LOOKS COLD.
- MM-HMM.

1735
01:12:36,387 --> 01:12:39,757
[SERVO SCATS
"RIDE OF THE VALKYRIES"]

1736
01:12:41,792 --> 01:12:44,293
PAMPLONA, SPAIN. THE ANNUAL
RUNNING OF THE GOATS!

1737
01:12:44,327 --> 01:12:47,563
[BOTS BAA]

1738
01:12:47,597 --> 01:12:50,900
THE CHRISTMAS
THAT ALMOST WASN'T.

1739
01:12:50,933 --> 01:12:54,137
IT'S NOT A FIT NIGHT OUT
FOR MAN OR BEAST.

1740
01:12:54,170 --> 01:12:55,672
THE DAY THE EARTH BECAME

1741
01:12:55,705 --> 01:12:59,175
UNSEASONABLY COOL.

1742
01:12:59,208 --> 01:13:01,043
I GUESS EVERYBODY'S
GOING TO BLAME ME

1743
01:13:01,078 --> 01:13:02,545
FOR THIS, TOO.

1744
01:13:02,578 --> 01:13:04,013
YEAH...WHAT?

1745
01:13:04,047 --> 01:13:07,083
OH, I THOUGHT
I CAULKED THAT THING.

1746
01:13:12,122 --> 01:13:13,723
LOOKS LIKE THEY MOVED IN
WITH THE INGALLS FAMILY.

1747
01:13:13,757 --> 01:13:15,392
YEAH, LITTLE HOUSE
ON THE TUNDRA.

1748
01:13:15,425 --> 01:13:18,395
[SERVO LAUGHS]

1749
01:13:18,428 --> 01:13:20,030
JEEZ. HAS TO HAVE

1750
01:13:20,063 --> 01:13:21,465
HALF AND HALF
WITH HER COFFEE.

1751
01:13:21,498 --> 01:13:23,667
OKAY, DEAR, I'LL WADE
THROUGH THE BLIZZARD

1752
01:13:23,700 --> 01:13:26,503
TO GET YOUR HALF AND HALF.

1753
01:13:26,537 --> 01:13:28,338
THE SHINING.

1754
01:13:31,208 --> 01:13:33,643
ACTUALLY, IT LOOKS
KIND OF INVITING.

1755
01:13:33,677 --> 01:13:36,313
♪ MOONLIGHT IN VERMONT ♪

1756
01:13:36,347 --> 01:13:38,248
♪ I'M GONNA BURY GARY ♪

1757
01:13:38,282 --> 01:13:41,785
♪ IN A PILE OF SNOW ♪

1758
01:13:41,818 --> 01:13:44,320
[SERVO HUMS]

1759
01:13:44,353 --> 01:13:46,390
AH, JEEZ,
ONE LITTLE CUP OF COFFEE,

1760
01:13:46,423 --> 01:13:48,892
AND SHE'S GOTTA HAVE
HER FRIGGIN' HALF AND HALF.

1761
01:13:48,925 --> 01:13:52,863
[SERVO GRUMBLES]

1762
01:13:52,897 --> 01:13:54,898
♪ WALKING IN MY
WINTER UNDERWEAR ♪

1763
01:13:54,932 --> 01:13:57,133
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1764
01:13:57,167 --> 01:14:00,203
HEY, A PENNY.

1765
01:14:00,237 --> 01:14:01,705
♪ WATCH OUT
WHERE THE HUSKIES GO ♪

1766
01:14:01,738 --> 01:14:05,075
♪ AND DON'T YOU EAT
THAT YELLOW SNOW ♪

1767
01:14:05,108 --> 01:14:07,643
UH, HEY, AUNT RODY?

1768
01:14:07,677 --> 01:14:10,180
THE OLD GREY GOOSE
IS DEAD.

1769
01:14:10,213 --> 01:14:13,350
ROSEBUD.

1770
01:14:18,722 --> 01:14:20,023
RIP TAYLOR'S OUTSIDE.

1771
01:14:20,057 --> 01:14:21,358
COME ON! I WANNA COME IN!

1772
01:14:21,392 --> 01:14:22,827
'CAUSE IT'S COLD OUTSIDE!

1773
01:14:22,860 --> 01:14:24,928
HAH! I GOT A BIG PROP
I WANNA SHOW YOU!

1774
01:14:24,962 --> 01:14:28,632
IT'S FUNNY!

1775
01:14:28,665 --> 01:14:30,800
IT'S TRUE.
FIRST DAY OF MARRIAGE

1776
01:14:30,833 --> 01:14:34,538
IS THE HARDEST.

1777
01:14:34,572 --> 01:14:37,040
HEY, HERE'S
YOUR DAMN DINNER.

1778
01:14:37,073 --> 01:14:39,242
HMM, I SUPPOSE YOU WANT ME

1779
01:14:39,275 --> 01:14:42,245
TO CLEAN THAT NOW.

1780
01:14:42,278 --> 01:14:44,213
I'M NOT THE PHEASANT
PLUCKER.

1781
01:14:44,247 --> 01:14:45,815
I'M THE PHEASANT
PLUCKER'S SON.

1782
01:14:45,848 --> 01:14:47,317
I'M ONLY PLUCKING
PHEASANTS

1783
01:14:47,350 --> 01:14:49,352
TILL THE PHEASANT
PLUCKER COMES.

1784
01:14:49,385 --> 01:14:51,455
I KNOW, DEAR. I KNOW.

1785
01:14:51,488 --> 01:14:54,190
UM... NOT ON THE GOOD BENCH.

1786
01:14:56,125 --> 01:14:59,362
HONEY, IT'S A SWAN'S
UNFROZEN DINNER.

1787
01:14:59,395 --> 01:15:01,665
- [CROW LAUGHS]
- OH, WHAT'S THE USE?

1788
01:15:01,698 --> 01:15:04,500
WE'LL CALL HER TRUDY.

1789
01:15:04,535 --> 01:15:06,237
WAIT, SHE'S WEARING
AN EMBROIDERY HOOP

1790
01:15:06,270 --> 01:15:08,072
ON HER HEAD.

1791
01:15:08,105 --> 01:15:09,873
ONE WORD. ANNULMENT.

1792
01:15:09,907 --> 01:15:12,042
I'M AFRAID THE POOR THING
IS DEAD.

1793
01:15:12,075 --> 01:15:13,577
OH, THE SAMPO
COULD'VE SAVED IT.

1794
01:15:13,610 --> 01:15:17,413
SHUT UP WITH THAT SAMPO!

1795
01:15:17,447 --> 01:15:19,950
SOON WE WILL ALL
BE LIKE THIS POOR BIRD.

1796
01:15:19,983 --> 01:15:21,485
[SERVO GROANS]

1797
01:15:21,518 --> 01:15:24,520
SHE'S TURNING INTO
A STEAK ON LEGS.

1798
01:15:24,555 --> 01:15:26,523
I CAN'T EVEN SEE
YOUR EYES, ANNIKKI.

1799
01:15:26,557 --> 01:15:28,958
WITHOUT THINKING OLIVES.

1800
01:15:28,992 --> 01:15:31,662
THAT'S THE WORST THING
ABOUT THIS TWILIGHT.

1801
01:15:31,695 --> 01:15:34,163
YOU'RE IN THE HOUSE.
TAKE YOUR BIKE HELMET OFF.

1802
01:15:34,197 --> 01:15:36,233
I CAN'T EVEN REMEMBER
WHAT COLOR THEY ARE.

1803
01:15:36,267 --> 01:15:38,102
LET ME LOOK
IN YOUR EYES AGAIN.

1804
01:15:38,135 --> 01:15:40,303
LOOK, SHE'S SWEDISH.
I'M GUESSING THEY'RE BLUE.

1805
01:15:40,337 --> 01:15:43,773
[ANNIKKI SOBS]

1806
01:15:43,807 --> 01:15:46,877
YEAH? WELL, I'M GONNA EAT.

1807
01:15:49,747 --> 01:15:52,648
HONEY, WE GOT ANY
ORANGE SAUCE IN THE HOUSE?

1808
01:15:52,682 --> 01:15:54,517
DUCK... WITH ORANGE.

1809
01:15:54,550 --> 01:15:57,553
DUCK WITH CHERRY.
A DUCK SURPRISE.

1810
01:15:57,587 --> 01:15:59,857
DUCK WITHOUT
ORANGE OR CHERRY.

1811
01:16:02,425 --> 01:16:03,893
ILLMARINEN!

1812
01:16:03,927 --> 01:16:06,228
HEY, WHAT'S THE DEAL
WITH YOUR SISTER, MAN?

1813
01:16:08,732 --> 01:16:10,733
- ILLMARINEN.
- D'AH-- HAMBURGERS!

1814
01:16:10,767 --> 01:16:13,470
OH, SORRY, DOZED OFF
ON THE OLD ANVIL.

1815
01:16:13,503 --> 01:16:16,907
- THIS--
- SUCKS.
- CANNOT GO ON MUCH LONGER.

1816
01:16:16,940 --> 01:16:20,110
YOU MUST MAKE
A NEW SUN FOR US.

1817
01:16:20,143 --> 01:16:21,878
I'LL USE THE SAMPO
TO MAKE ONE.

1818
01:16:21,912 --> 01:16:23,147
OH, WAIT, WE DON'T HAVE ONE.

1819
01:16:23,180 --> 01:16:26,617
THAT'S RIGHT.

1820
01:16:26,650 --> 01:16:28,618
I WILL DO WHAT I CAN.

1821
01:16:28,652 --> 01:16:30,153
NOT AS I DO.

1822
01:16:30,187 --> 01:16:31,888
HUH. GRANDPA RIOTED

1823
01:16:31,922 --> 01:16:34,490
AND GOT A WEEK IN THE HOLE.

1824
01:16:34,523 --> 01:16:36,760
THE GREAT ESCAPE,
30 YEARS LATER.

1825
01:16:36,793 --> 01:16:39,328
[SERVO HUMS GREAT ESCAPE THEME]

1826
01:16:41,097 --> 01:16:43,433
[CROW YAWNS]

1827
01:16:43,467 --> 01:16:44,968
WELL, I'M TURNING IN.

1828
01:16:45,002 --> 01:16:46,737
BIG DAY.

1829
01:16:50,373 --> 01:16:52,775
[ALL]
♪ FA-HOO FORES ♪

1830
01:16:52,808 --> 01:16:55,345
♪ DA-HOO DORES ♪

1831
01:16:55,378 --> 01:16:58,882
♪ WELCOME... ♪

1832
01:16:58,915 --> 01:17:00,517
WHY ARE THEY SO BUMMED OUT?

1833
01:17:00,550 --> 01:17:02,518
OH, THEY JUST
SAW CAPTAIN RON.

1834
01:17:02,552 --> 01:17:04,420
OH.

1835
01:17:04,453 --> 01:17:06,557
PERSONALLY,
I LIKE KURT RUSSELL.

1836
01:17:06,590 --> 01:17:08,792
I LOVED THE COMPUTER
WORE TENNIS SHOES,

1837
01:17:08,825 --> 01:17:11,160
BUT THAT'S JUST ME.

1838
01:17:11,193 --> 01:17:12,862
NO, NO, THE SUN'S BIGGER.

1839
01:17:12,895 --> 01:17:15,265
YES, WE RECALL
IT BEING QUITE LARGE.

1840
01:17:15,298 --> 01:17:16,733
AND IT'S GOT--
IT'S GOT SPOTS.

1841
01:17:16,767 --> 01:17:18,035
- MM-HMM.
- YES.

1842
01:17:18,068 --> 01:17:20,070
WHAT'RE YOU DOING,
ILLMARINEN?

1843
01:17:20,103 --> 01:17:23,540
HE IS FORGING
A NEW SUN FOR US.

1844
01:17:23,573 --> 01:17:25,708
- THIS IS FUTILE.
- NO, IT'S FUSION.

1845
01:17:25,742 --> 01:17:28,812
TRYING TO FORGE
THE SUN ANEW?

1846
01:17:28,845 --> 01:17:31,748
THE ONE THING LEFT
IS TO RELEASE IT FROM PRISON.

1847
01:17:31,782 --> 01:17:33,750
WELL THEN, YOU COME UP
WITH YOUR OWN IDEAS, MAN.

1848
01:17:33,783 --> 01:17:35,252
TAKE UP YOUR SWORDS.

1849
01:17:35,285 --> 01:17:38,322
YOUR SWORDS AND SPEARS.

1850
01:17:38,355 --> 01:17:41,592
VAINAMOINEN WILL
LEAD US TO POHJOLA.

1851
01:17:41,625 --> 01:17:43,593
- YEAH.
- AND WE SHALL
FIGHT A BATTLE

1852
01:17:43,627 --> 01:17:45,228
TO RELEASE THE SUN.

1853
01:17:45,262 --> 01:17:46,563
NOT SO, LEMMINKAINEN.

1854
01:17:46,597 --> 01:17:49,298
HAVE A SEAT, LEM.

1855
01:17:49,332 --> 01:17:52,768
YOU CANNOT PREVAIL
WITH A SWORD.

1856
01:17:52,802 --> 01:17:55,105
OF WHAT USE ARE YOUR SWORDS

1857
01:17:55,138 --> 01:17:57,407
AGAINST THEIR SPELLS?

1858
01:17:57,440 --> 01:17:59,810
I WILL TAKE
ALL OF YOU TO POHJOLA.

1859
01:17:59,843 --> 01:18:01,110
A CLASS TRIP?

1860
01:18:01,143 --> 01:18:02,712
AND EACH ONE OF YOU
MUST HOLD--

1861
01:18:02,745 --> 01:18:03,980
A HERRING!

1862
01:18:04,013 --> 01:18:06,215
- IN PLACE OF A SPEAR--
- OH.

1863
01:18:06,248 --> 01:18:08,885
- OR A BLADE
- YOU'RE MAKING THIS UP,
AREN'T YOU?

1864
01:18:08,918 --> 01:18:12,622
- A SWEETLY-SOUNDING--
- IT'S!

1865
01:18:12,655 --> 01:18:14,390
KANTALE.

1866
01:18:14,423 --> 01:18:16,827
I DON'T KNOW. JUST MAD.

1867
01:18:16,860 --> 01:18:18,362
AND IF EACH OF US
CARRY ONE OF THEM,

1868
01:18:18,395 --> 01:18:20,230
THAT'S A THOUSAND KANTALES.

1869
01:18:20,263 --> 01:18:22,998
- MORE THAN THAT.
- 1,200 AT LEAST.

1870
01:18:23,032 --> 01:18:24,868
--WE HAVE THEM.

1871
01:18:24,902 --> 01:18:27,837
HERE IN THESE
ANCIENT PINE TREES.

1872
01:18:27,870 --> 01:18:30,273
WE'LL CUT THEM DOWN.

1873
01:18:30,307 --> 01:18:31,875
MAKE THE HARPS OURSELVES.

1874
01:18:31,908 --> 01:18:35,778
GREAT. WE SPEND THE WINTER
MAKING HARPS.

1875
01:18:35,812 --> 01:18:38,682
WHAT'RE YOU LOOKING AT?

1876
01:18:38,715 --> 01:18:42,285
TAKE ALL THE BOATS DOWN
TO THE SHORES OF THE FROZEN SEA.

1877
01:18:42,318 --> 01:18:44,553
WHATEVER.

1878
01:18:44,587 --> 01:18:47,023
- AND YOU WOMEN.
- BACK ME UP ON THIS ONE.

1879
01:18:47,057 --> 01:18:50,660
TAKE ALL YOUR JEWELRY
OF SILVER AND GOLD.

1880
01:18:50,693 --> 01:18:52,895
ALL YOUR EARRINGS.
ALL YOUR BRACELETS.

1881
01:18:52,928 --> 01:18:54,563
ALL YOUR NAUGHTY THINGS.

1882
01:18:54,597 --> 01:18:57,133
--INTO THE CRUCIBLE
OF ILLMARINEN.

1883
01:18:57,167 --> 01:18:59,970
HE MUST HAVE
CLEAR-SOUNDING STRINGS

1884
01:19:00,003 --> 01:19:01,905
FOR OUR KANTALES.

1885
01:19:01,938 --> 01:19:04,673
YEAH? FIRST HE HAS US
MAKING BOATS,

1886
01:19:04,707 --> 01:19:05,942
THEN WE GOTTA DO THE HORSE.

1887
01:19:05,975 --> 01:19:08,578
NOW IT'S THE KANTALES. AH.

1888
01:19:08,612 --> 01:19:10,480
THIS IS THE OLD GUY'S NECK.

1889
01:19:10,513 --> 01:19:12,648
THIS IS HIS HEAD.

1890
01:19:12,682 --> 01:19:14,650
AND THIS IS HIS RIBCAGE.

1891
01:19:14,683 --> 01:19:16,218
WOW, HE'S GOT
THE FARRAH FAWCETT

1892
01:19:16,252 --> 01:19:20,157
EXERCISE STICK OVER THERE.

1893
01:19:20,190 --> 01:19:21,725
OKAY, WHO WANTS A HOT DOG?

1894
01:19:21,758 --> 01:19:22,958
STILL GONNA BE
A COUPLE OF MINUTES

1895
01:19:22,992 --> 01:19:24,693
ON THE BRATS.
JUST KEEP THIS BURNT ONE

1896
01:19:24,727 --> 01:19:26,395
FOR ME TO NIBBLE ON.

1897
01:19:26,428 --> 01:19:29,198
HONEY, WHY DON'T YOU GO GET
THOSE MARINATED STEAKS READY?

1898
01:19:31,433 --> 01:19:33,270
AL, COME ON.
DON'T BE TOO CAREFUL.

1899
01:19:33,303 --> 01:19:36,238
WE JUST GOTTA
KNOCK OUT THESE KANTALES.

1900
01:19:36,272 --> 01:19:37,773
[CROW GROANS]

1901
01:19:37,807 --> 01:19:41,443
OW! CARVED MY OWN LEG
INTO A KANTALE.

1902
01:19:41,478 --> 01:19:42,778
HEY, UH, ANYBODY CARE

1903
01:19:42,812 --> 01:19:46,382
IF I TURN ON THE RADIO?

1904
01:19:46,415 --> 01:19:48,152
HUH. CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

1905
01:19:48,185 --> 01:19:50,987
TWO WEEKS AGO, WE WERE
IN SHORTS OUT HERE.

1906
01:19:53,590 --> 01:19:56,960
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
THE MORMON TABERNACLE CHOIR
AND MOUNTAIN BOYS!

1907
01:19:56,993 --> 01:19:58,728
UH, CROW,
YOU ARE OUT THERE, MAN.

1908
01:19:58,762 --> 01:20:00,963
THANK YOU.

1909
01:20:00,997 --> 01:20:02,398
[JOEL GROANS]

1910
01:20:02,432 --> 01:20:04,267
BUT GERMAN POTATO SALAD

1911
01:20:04,300 --> 01:20:07,870
TAKES A LITTLE LONGER.

1912
01:20:07,903 --> 01:20:09,940
IT'S A BOY!

1913
01:20:09,973 --> 01:20:11,708
[ALL QUACK]

1914
01:20:22,218 --> 01:20:23,953
OH, WELL, THE ICE SEEMS SAFE.

1915
01:20:23,987 --> 01:20:25,355
WE SHOULD'VE
BROUGHT THE PICKUP.

1916
01:20:25,388 --> 01:20:26,790
OH, GOLLY.

1917
01:20:26,823 --> 01:20:28,592
[ALL]
CIGARS? CIGARETTES?

1918
01:20:28,625 --> 01:20:31,460
CIGARS? CIGARETTES?

1919
01:20:31,493 --> 01:20:35,332
WE COME BEARING
HONEY-BAKED HAMS.

1920
01:20:35,365 --> 01:20:37,367
TELL ME,
MY FEARSOME WIZARDS--

1921
01:20:37,400 --> 01:20:39,102
OKAY, YOU'RE UGLY,
AND YOU SMELL BAD.

1922
01:20:39,135 --> 01:20:41,103
WHAT HAVE WE HERE?

1923
01:20:41,137 --> 01:20:44,407
UH, IT'S AN ARMY OF WARRIORS
FROM KALEVALA.

1924
01:20:44,440 --> 01:20:46,777
- KALELALALA?
- AND THEY'RE ALL
COMING THIS WAY.

1925
01:20:46,810 --> 01:20:48,578
AND THERE'S TOO MANY
OF THEM TO COUNT!

1926
01:20:48,612 --> 01:20:51,113
THE YEAR MY VOICE BROKE!

1927
01:20:52,848 --> 01:20:55,552
COME ON, WE WANT THE SUN!

1928
01:20:55,585 --> 01:20:57,787
[ALL]
WE WANT THE SUN!

1929
01:20:57,820 --> 01:20:59,055
OH.

1930
01:20:59,088 --> 01:21:00,823
WHEN KINGS GO SENILE.

1931
01:21:00,857 --> 01:21:02,958
I THOUGHT IT WAS
A COSTUME BALL!

1932
01:21:02,992 --> 01:21:05,195
THEY'RE GONNA LAUNCH HIM
FROM A CATAPULT?

1933
01:21:05,228 --> 01:21:07,097
[SERVO MIMICS DRUMROLL]

1934
01:21:07,130 --> 01:21:09,265
WHAT WEAPONS DO THEY CARRY?

1935
01:21:09,298 --> 01:21:11,467
- HARPS.
- HARPS.

1936
01:21:11,500 --> 01:21:13,002
I WONDER, DO THEY THINK

1937
01:21:13,035 --> 01:21:15,205
THEY'RE COMING
TO A WEDDING FEAST?

1938
01:21:15,238 --> 01:21:17,707
HA-HA! GOOD ONE,
YOUR HIDEOUSNESS.

1939
01:21:17,740 --> 01:21:19,675
LIKED IT. LIKED IT.

1940
01:21:19,708 --> 01:21:22,312
♪♪ [PLAYS KANTALE]

1941
01:21:22,345 --> 01:21:24,347
L-- ♪ LOVE ♪

1942
01:21:24,380 --> 01:21:27,317
♪ SOFT AS AN EASY CHAIR ♪

1943
01:21:29,485 --> 01:21:31,053
TAKE UP YOUR SPEARS!

1944
01:21:31,087 --> 01:21:32,788
THE ONES POINTED
WITH SHARK'S TEETH.

1945
01:21:32,822 --> 01:21:35,658
UH, SURE, AS SOON AS
THIS TUNE IS OVER.

1946
01:21:35,692 --> 01:21:37,560
--STEEPED IN SERPENT'S VENOM

1947
01:21:37,593 --> 01:21:39,762
AND KILL EVERY ONE OF THEM!

1948
01:21:39,795 --> 01:21:43,232
UH, DID YOU HEAR THAT, SIR?

1949
01:21:43,267 --> 01:21:47,070
KILL THEM ALL!

1950
01:21:47,103 --> 01:21:49,372
YOU KNOW, THE MUSIC KINDA
ADDS TO THE DRAMA, ACTUALLY.

1951
01:21:49,405 --> 01:21:52,008
- IT DOES.
- IT'S ALL-SKATE.

1952
01:21:52,042 --> 01:21:55,245
EVERYBODY ON THE ICE.
ALL-SKATE.

1953
01:21:55,278 --> 01:21:58,180
STALINGRAD.
THE STANDOFF DRAGGED ON.

1954
01:22:00,350 --> 01:22:03,387
DON'T LISTEN TO THAT MUSIC!

1955
01:22:03,420 --> 01:22:05,155
WAKE UP! COVER YOUR EARS!

1956
01:22:05,188 --> 01:22:07,757
COVER THEM UP
WITH YOUR HANDS!

1957
01:22:07,790 --> 01:22:10,460
THAT TERRIBLE MUSIC
WILL KILL US ALL.

1958
01:22:10,493 --> 01:22:12,362
YEAH, WELL, WE PUT UP
WITH YOUR KENNY G,

1959
01:22:12,395 --> 01:22:14,430
YOU... COW.

1960
01:22:14,463 --> 01:22:18,100
WELCOME TO THE MOODY BIBLE
INSTITUTE PRAYER HOUR.

1961
01:22:18,133 --> 01:22:21,137
UH, GRANDPA,
TRY ANOTHER CHORD.

1962
01:22:22,705 --> 01:22:24,707
HE'S DOING
SELF-INDULGENT JAM.

1963
01:22:24,740 --> 01:22:28,110
--STOP THEM!
GET YOUR SWORDS OUT!

1964
01:22:28,143 --> 01:22:29,478
USE YOUR KNIFE!

1965
01:22:29,512 --> 01:22:31,447
MM, FOR ONCE,
I'M ON HER SIDE.

1966
01:22:31,480 --> 01:22:34,750
USE YOUR ARROWS!

1967
01:22:34,783 --> 01:22:36,920
UNSHEATHE YOUR BROADSWORDS!

1968
01:22:36,953 --> 01:22:38,722
ATTACK THEM! ATTACK THEM!

1969
01:22:38,755 --> 01:22:41,157
UGH, BUT I LOVE
PRAIRIE HOME COMPANION.

1970
01:22:41,190 --> 01:22:44,027
ANY TIME I CAN SIT AND LISTEN,
I LOVE IT.

1971
01:22:46,528 --> 01:22:48,465
- [CROW SNORES]
- AND THAT'S THE NEWS
FROM LAKE WOBEGON,

1972
01:22:48,498 --> 01:22:50,733
WHERE THE MEN ARE STRONG,
THE WOMEN ARE GOOD-LOOKING,

1973
01:22:50,767 --> 01:22:53,135
AND THE CHILDREN
ARE ABOVE-AVERAGE.

1974
01:22:53,168 --> 01:22:55,472
OH, BUTCH THOMPSON'S GONNA
COME OUT WITH THE BAND.

1975
01:22:55,505 --> 01:22:57,873
- [JOEL AND CROW SNORE]
- GONNA DO A MEDLEY
OF SONGS ABOUT CATS.

1976
01:22:57,907 --> 01:23:00,943
THEN JIM ED POOLE
WILL DO SOME CAT SOUNDS,

1977
01:23:00,977 --> 01:23:03,580
AND THEN ANOTHER EPISODE
OF "WATCHING PAINT DRY."

1978
01:23:03,613 --> 01:23:05,215
THEN CLAUDIA SCHMIDT'LL
COME OUT

1979
01:23:05,248 --> 01:23:06,983
AND TRY TO FILL
THE GAP IN HER TEETH.

1980
01:23:07,017 --> 01:23:09,218
AH, THEN PAT DONOHUE
AND PETER OSTROUSHKO

1981
01:23:09,252 --> 01:23:10,720
ARE GONNA FAVOR US
WITH THE STORY

1982
01:23:10,753 --> 01:23:13,122
OF THE SWEDE WHO
DIDN'T LIKE MEATBALLS.

1983
01:23:13,155 --> 01:23:14,457
THEN, UH...

1984
01:23:14,490 --> 01:23:16,258
AH, IT'S SO HARD TO GET

1985
01:23:16,292 --> 01:23:20,097
GOOD TROLLS THESE DAYS.

1986
01:23:20,130 --> 01:23:22,032
OH, IT'S A MAPPLETHORPE
PHOTO.

1987
01:23:22,065 --> 01:23:25,102
GO FORTH, NORTH WIND!
GO FORTH!

1988
01:23:25,135 --> 01:23:27,670
FREEZE THE PEOPLE
OF KALEVALA!

1989
01:23:27,703 --> 01:23:30,407
SHROUD THEM IN
THE MANTLE OF DEATH!

1990
01:23:30,440 --> 01:23:33,175
[SERVO HISSES]

1991
01:23:33,208 --> 01:23:34,543
DON'T LOOK AT IT, MARION!

1992
01:23:34,577 --> 01:23:36,947
DON'T LOOK!

1993
01:23:40,183 --> 01:23:44,053
I SAID, "HARP FASTER!"

1994
01:23:44,087 --> 01:23:47,623
LET'S KICK INTO
OUR GRAND FUNK MEDLEY!

1995
01:23:48,858 --> 01:23:51,828
UM... UM, SIR,
MAYBE IT'S TIME

1996
01:23:51,862 --> 01:23:54,663
TO BREAK OUT THE BAGPIPES.

1997
01:23:54,697 --> 01:23:55,998
OOH!

1998
01:23:56,032 --> 01:23:58,067
I SAY, I HEAR THEY

1999
01:23:58,100 --> 01:23:59,735
CALL IT MARIAH.

2000
01:23:59,768 --> 01:24:01,972
WELL, WHATEVER IT IS,
IT'S FLIPPIN' FREEZING!

2001
01:24:02,005 --> 01:24:03,840
YEP!

2002
01:24:03,873 --> 01:24:06,575
OKAY, UH,
DO YOU HAVE A PLAN B?

2003
01:24:06,608 --> 01:24:08,143
ALL RIGHT, NEW TUNE.
EVERYBODY.

2004
01:24:08,177 --> 01:24:12,115
A ONE, A TWO, A ONE--
OH, FORGET IT.

2005
01:24:12,148 --> 01:24:13,483
HEH, IT'S PATTON.

2006
01:24:13,517 --> 01:24:16,118
YOU DO NOT BELONG
IN THIS PLACE OF HONOR!

2007
01:24:20,523 --> 01:24:23,827
♪ 'TWAS A ROCK AND ROLL
CREATION! ♪

2008
01:24:28,532 --> 01:24:30,900
YEAH, CREAM OF WHEAT
STAYS WITH YOU ALL DAY,

2009
01:24:30,933 --> 01:24:33,235
AND THAT'S NICE.

2010
01:24:36,005 --> 01:24:39,342
KIND OF LILTING, ISN'T IT?

2011
01:24:39,375 --> 01:24:41,043
GO FORTH, MY CLOAK,

2012
01:24:41,077 --> 01:24:43,447
- TO THE ARMY OF KALEVALA--
- KALEVALALALA.

2013
01:24:43,480 --> 01:24:46,215
- AND STRANGLE THOSE WARRIORS
- YEP, STRANGLE. WARRIORS.

2014
01:24:46,248 --> 01:24:48,117
WHO STILL REMAIN
ON THEIR FEET.

2015
01:24:48,150 --> 01:24:51,553
AND FEET. RIGHT. OKAY, BYE.

2016
01:24:51,587 --> 01:24:54,723
SOUNDTRACK BY SPIKE JONES.

2017
01:24:54,757 --> 01:24:56,158
HEY, THROW ME THE CAPE--

2018
01:24:56,192 --> 01:25:00,028
OH. D'OH.

2019
01:25:00,062 --> 01:25:02,832
UH, UH, ANYBODY WANNA
THROW IN HERE?

2020
01:25:05,702 --> 01:25:07,170
THIS HAS GOTTA BE
EMBARRASSING.

2021
01:25:07,203 --> 01:25:09,638
YEAH, ON TOP OF THE WHOLE
SAMPO EPISODE EARLIER.

2022
01:25:09,672 --> 01:25:12,475
OOH, YEAH.

2023
01:25:12,508 --> 01:25:14,943
UGH, CLOAK
TOOK ADVANTAGE OF ME.

2024
01:25:20,683 --> 01:25:22,852
WE THOUGHT THE CLOAK
MIGHT TRY SOMETHING LIKE THIS.

2025
01:25:22,885 --> 01:25:25,788
- WE WERE PREPARED.
- YEP.

2026
01:25:25,822 --> 01:25:28,057
LOOK AT THAT.

2027
01:25:28,090 --> 01:25:29,392
OH, IT'S RUINED
'CAUSE IT SAID

2028
01:25:29,425 --> 01:25:32,795
"HAND WASH ONLY"
IN COLD WATER.

2029
01:25:32,828 --> 01:25:34,230
STUPID CLOAK.

2030
01:25:34,263 --> 01:25:36,265
STUPID, DUMB OLD JERK CLOAK.

2031
01:25:36,298 --> 01:25:39,468
SNOT... STUPID.

2032
01:25:39,502 --> 01:25:41,637
I'M ALL YOURS, SIR.
SORRY ABOUT THAT.

2033
01:25:41,670 --> 01:25:43,973
NOW, LEMMINKAINEN, YOU SEE?

2034
01:25:44,007 --> 01:25:46,542
NOW YOU MAY GO IN
AND SET THE SUN FREE!

2035
01:25:46,575 --> 01:25:48,978
OH, MAY I?

2036
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:54,317
- UH, THIS THING HERE?
- YES!

2037
01:25:54,350 --> 01:25:56,118
GLORY OF KALEVALA!

2038
01:25:56,152 --> 01:25:58,722
I AM GOING TO RELEASE
THE SUN FROM THE--

2039
01:25:58,755 --> 01:26:01,290
OH, JUST DO IT,
AND DON'T SCREW IT UP!

2040
01:26:01,323 --> 01:26:03,292
REMEMBER THE SAMPO, BUDDY.

2041
01:26:03,325 --> 01:26:05,060
NO, WHAT DO YOU WANT?

2042
01:26:05,093 --> 01:26:07,597
KEEP AWAY! KEEP AWAY!

2043
01:26:07,630 --> 01:26:10,165
OH, THE PAIN! THE PAIN.

2044
01:26:10,200 --> 01:26:12,335
OH, WELL, THAT MAKES IT
A LOT EASIER.

2045
01:26:12,368 --> 01:26:15,170
HEY, MRS. WITCH, CAN YOUR SUN
COME OUT AND PLAY?

2046
01:26:17,473 --> 01:26:19,408
OOH.

2047
01:26:21,477 --> 01:26:23,212
HEY.

2048
01:26:23,245 --> 01:26:25,215
HEY, YOU KNOW, YOU DON'T LIKE
THE WEATHER IN SWEDEN?

2049
01:26:25,248 --> 01:26:26,715
- JUST WAIT A MINUTE, YOU KNOW?
- [CROW LAUGHS]

2050
01:26:26,748 --> 01:26:29,052
SWEDE BLANKET BINGO!

2051
01:26:29,085 --> 01:26:32,388
I'LL TAKE SWEDEN, WOW!

2052
01:26:32,422 --> 01:26:34,623
SO THEY HEADED FOR
CENTRAL MINNESOTA, YOU KNOW,

2053
01:26:34,657 --> 01:26:36,825
TO BUILD CRYSTAL
AND BLAINE AND FRIDLEY.

2054
01:26:36,858 --> 01:26:38,227
AND THEY MADE BARS
AND SOUGHT OUT

2055
01:26:38,260 --> 01:26:41,932
CHURCH BASEMENTS
FOR REFUGE, AND...

2056
01:26:41,965 --> 01:26:45,067
OH, LET'S SEE IF THE TORGELSONS
WANT TO HAVE A LUAU TONIGHT.

2057
01:26:45,100 --> 01:26:47,103
YEAH, THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.

2058
01:26:47,137 --> 01:26:48,605
WELCOME, GREG ALLMAN!

2059
01:26:48,638 --> 01:26:50,507
HI.

2060
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:52,108
AND WELCOME, ROGER McGUINN!

2061
01:26:52,142 --> 01:26:53,977
HOWDY.

2062
01:26:54,010 --> 01:26:56,947
THIS IS THE MOST EMOTION
EVER EXPRESSED IN SWEDEN,

2063
01:26:56,980 --> 01:26:59,582
- YOU REALIZE THAT?
- I DID THE SUN THING, OKAY?

2064
01:27:03,385 --> 01:27:06,055
THANK YOU, LEATHERHEAD.

2065
01:27:06,088 --> 01:27:09,325
[BOTS CHUCKLE]

2066
01:27:09,358 --> 01:27:11,060
MAY THERE ALWAYS BE...

2067
01:27:11,093 --> 01:27:13,195
IT'S YOU!
YOU BROUGHT THE BIRDS!

2068
01:27:13,228 --> 01:27:14,530
YOU'RE EVIL!

2069
01:27:14,563 --> 01:27:15,998
IT'S THE END OF THE WORLD.

2070
01:27:16,032 --> 01:27:19,235
--ALWAYS BE LOVE
IN THE WORLD.

2071
01:27:19,268 --> 01:27:21,670
AH... OKAY.

2072
01:27:25,642 --> 01:27:27,577
LEMMINKAINEN AND ANNIKKI
WILL BE BACK

2073
01:27:27,610 --> 01:27:30,947
IN THE FORESTS
OF SECRETS AND LIES.

2074
01:27:34,283 --> 01:27:36,252
NEAT, HUH?

2075
01:27:36,285 --> 01:27:38,855
LEMMINKAINEN WAS
PLAYED BY JOHN POWERS.

2076
01:27:38,888 --> 01:27:42,825
NOT VERY WELL, GRANTED.

2077
01:27:42,858 --> 01:27:44,893
ANNIKKI BY NINA ANDERSON.

2078
01:27:44,927 --> 01:27:46,262
DONATIONS ARE BEING ACCEPTED

2079
01:27:46,295 --> 01:27:49,498
AT THE STOCKHOLM
SPINAL RESEARCH HOSPITAL.

2080
01:27:49,532 --> 01:27:51,968
LOUHI THE WITCH,
BY INGRID ELHARDT.

2081
01:27:52,002 --> 01:27:54,370
A WOMAN? YES, A WOMAN.

2082
01:27:54,403 --> 01:27:56,605
ILLMARINEN
BY PETER SORENSON.

2083
01:27:56,638 --> 01:27:58,607
KNOW THESE FACES,
REMEMBER THESE NAMES.

2084
01:27:58,642 --> 01:28:00,943
VAINAMOINEN BY ELGIN TANNER.

2085
01:28:00,977 --> 01:28:02,612
JAMES AT 92.

2086
01:28:02,645 --> 01:28:04,380
IF YOU SEE
ANY OF THESE PEOPLE,

2087
01:28:04,413 --> 01:28:06,615
PLEASE, FOR THEIR OWN SAKES,
TURN THEM IN.

2088
01:28:06,648 --> 01:28:10,420
- WELL SAID.
- ♪ FINLAND FINLAND FINLAND ♪

2089
01:28:20,497 --> 01:28:22,598
YOU KNOW, GYPSY,
I JUST WANTED TO TELL YOU

2090
01:28:22,632 --> 01:28:24,900
HOW MUCH I ENJOYED
YOUR ONE-WOMAN SHOW EARLIER.

2091
01:28:24,933 --> 01:28:26,735
YOU KNOW,
IT WAS SO CONFESSIONAL.

2092
01:28:26,768 --> 01:28:29,405
THERE WERE TIMES I ACTUALLY
FELT KIND OF UNCOMFORTABLE.

2093
01:28:29,438 --> 01:28:31,107
OH, GREAT, YOU KNOW,
IF YOU HADN'T,

2094
01:28:31,140 --> 01:28:33,208
I WOULD'VE FELT I'D FAILED.

2095
01:28:33,242 --> 01:28:35,310
WELL, I GOTTA GO
RINSE SOME THINGS.

2096
01:28:35,345 --> 01:28:37,813
OKAY. SEE YOU LATER.

2097
01:28:37,847 --> 01:28:39,415
HEY...

2098
01:28:39,448 --> 01:28:40,917
WHAT'RE YOU GUYS DOING?

2099
01:28:40,950 --> 01:28:42,852
- GUESS!
- UM...

2100
01:28:42,885 --> 01:28:44,487
- GIVE UP?
- NO, YOU'RE--

2101
01:28:44,520 --> 01:28:46,355
YOU'RE THE WIND
FROM TODAY'S MOVIE.

2102
01:28:46,388 --> 01:28:48,958
NICE SIMPLISTIC
ANSWER, JOEL.

2103
01:28:48,992 --> 01:28:51,160
BUT WE'VE GONE BEYOND THAT.

2104
01:28:51,193 --> 01:28:53,328
WE ARE DELICATELY
WAFTING SCENTS

2105
01:28:53,362 --> 01:28:55,063
STRICTLY BORN BY THE WIND

2106
01:28:55,097 --> 01:28:57,533
AND CARESSING
YOUR ROSY CHEEK.

2107
01:28:57,567 --> 01:28:58,802
MM, OKAY.

2108
01:28:58,835 --> 01:29:01,937
FOR EXAMPLE,
I'M A LILAC IN THE SPRING.

2109
01:29:01,970 --> 01:29:03,205
[SERVO GROWLS]

2110
01:29:03,238 --> 01:29:05,842
- I'M A SLICE OF PIE.
- NICE, UH,

2111
01:29:05,875 --> 01:29:07,410
CREATIVE IDEA.

2112
01:29:07,443 --> 01:29:10,045
- OR I COULD BE A PIZZA.
- OH, YEAH, WITH ONIONS

2113
01:29:10,078 --> 01:29:11,813
AND A KIND OF LOW-GRADE
BUDGET SAUSAGE.

2114
01:29:11,847 --> 01:29:13,082
SURE, SURE. YEAH.

2115
01:29:13,115 --> 01:29:14,717
YOU KNOW, I SUPPOSE
I COULD BE THE WIND,

2116
01:29:14,750 --> 01:29:16,918
BUT I'D BE THE WIND
THAT COMES FROM YOUR FRIEND

2117
01:29:16,952 --> 01:29:19,388
WHO MANAGES THE RIALTO THEATER,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

2118
01:29:19,422 --> 01:29:21,557
AND I'M THE STENCH
OF BITTER FAILURE.

2119
01:29:21,590 --> 01:29:24,493
I'M JAMES COCO'S
OLDEST PAIR OF BOXER SHORTS.

2120
01:29:24,527 --> 01:29:25,895
I'M DICK BUTKUS!

2121
01:29:25,928 --> 01:29:27,463
OH, OKAY. OKAY, YOU TWO.

2122
01:29:27,497 --> 01:29:29,432
I THINK IT'S TIME FOR US
TO READ A LETTER.

2123
01:29:29,465 --> 01:29:31,267
OKAY? LET'S JUST...

2124
01:29:31,300 --> 01:29:32,602
HEY! WHAT WAS THAT!

2125
01:29:32,635 --> 01:29:34,037
IT SOUNDED
LIKE FABRIC TEARING!

2126
01:29:34,070 --> 01:29:35,605
- WE'RE GOING DOWN!
- I'M JUST-- I'M JUST--

2127
01:29:35,638 --> 01:29:37,107
I'M JUST-- HEY! I'M JUST--

2128
01:29:37,140 --> 01:29:39,575
I'M JUST OPENING
THE MAIL BAG, OKAY?

2129
01:29:39,608 --> 01:29:40,843
HERE'S A LETTER. UH,

2130
01:29:40,877 --> 01:29:42,612
LET'S PUT THAT UP
ON STILL STORE, CAMBOT.

2131
01:29:42,645 --> 01:29:44,380
- AND THERE'S A PICTURE.
- A PICTURE.

2132
01:29:44,413 --> 01:29:47,317
UM, THIS ONE COMES FROM
A DONNA SWEENEY

2133
01:29:47,350 --> 01:29:48,717
- HELLO, DONNA!
- AND SHE SAYS,

2134
01:29:48,752 --> 01:29:51,120
"I JUST WANT TO TELL YOU THAT
MY HUSBAND BRIAN AND I

2135
01:29:51,153 --> 01:29:53,155
"ARE THE BIGGEST
MST3000 FANS

2136
01:29:53,188 --> 01:29:55,090
AND HAVE BEEN SO
FOR MANY YEARS."

2137
01:29:55,123 --> 01:29:56,992
- THANK YOU.
- "CURRENTLY MY HUSBAND AND I

2138
01:29:57,025 --> 01:29:58,828
RESIDE IN GERMANY."

2139
01:29:58,862 --> 01:30:00,497
- AH, GERMANY.
- UM,

2140
01:30:00,530 --> 01:30:02,532
"MY HUSBAND IS AN ARMY

2141
01:30:02,565 --> 01:30:04,867
"BOMB DISPOSAL EXPERT.

2142
01:30:04,900 --> 01:30:06,702
"I AM ENCLOSING A PHOTO

2143
01:30:06,735 --> 01:30:08,938
"OF THEIR
BOMB DISPOSAL ROBOT

2144
01:30:08,972 --> 01:30:10,405
"AND I WANT TO LET YOU KNOW

2145
01:30:10,440 --> 01:30:12,242
"THAT HE HAS BEEN
NICKNAMED CROW

2146
01:30:12,275 --> 01:30:14,210
- [BOTS] HUH?
- IN HONOR OF CROW T. ROBOT.

2147
01:30:14,243 --> 01:30:15,812
- HEY. LET ME SEE THAT.
- WHAT THE--

2148
01:30:15,845 --> 01:30:17,247
THAT IS PRETTY NEAT.

2149
01:30:17,280 --> 01:30:19,382
I THINK I SHOULD SHOW THIS
TO GYPSY. SHE'D PROBABLY

2150
01:30:19,415 --> 01:30:20,717
- REALLY LIKE IT.
- HEY, HEY! HELP US DOWN!

2151
01:30:20,750 --> 01:30:22,418
I'D LIKE TO SEE THAT!
JOEL! JOEL!

2152
01:30:22,452 --> 01:30:23,718
CAN YOU GIVE US A HAND?
WE REALLY WANT

2153
01:30:23,752 --> 01:30:25,988
TO COME DOWN NOW. D'OH.

2154
01:30:26,022 --> 01:30:28,057
UM, JOEL, I-- YOU MIGHT
WANT TO HELP US DOWN,

2155
01:30:28,090 --> 01:30:29,525
'CAUSE WE SMELL
REALLY GOOD NOW.

2156
01:30:29,558 --> 01:30:31,360
I'M A T.J. CINNAMON BUN.

2157
01:30:31,393 --> 01:30:33,362
UH, I'M NOT INTERESTED.

2158
01:30:33,395 --> 01:30:35,565
AND I'M FRESH APPLESAUCE--

2159
01:30:35,598 --> 01:30:37,167
OH, HE'S GONE.

2160
01:30:37,200 --> 01:30:39,735
- UH, THINK HE'LL BE BACK?
- I DON'T KNOW.

2161
01:30:39,768 --> 01:30:41,337
HEY, WHAT'S YOUR BAG
SMELL LIKE?

2162
01:30:41,370 --> 01:30:42,672
OH, YOU DON'T WANNA KNOW.

2163
01:30:42,705 --> 01:30:44,407
[BOTH GROAN]

2164
01:30:44,440 --> 01:30:45,908
FRANK, ARE YOU
ALL RIGHT UP THERE?

2165
01:30:45,942 --> 01:30:47,210
WHAT DO YOU CARE?

2166
01:30:47,243 --> 01:30:48,710
FRANK. I CARE A LOT.

2167
01:30:48,743 --> 01:30:49,978
THEN GIVE ME BACK MY MONEY.

2168
01:30:50,012 --> 01:30:51,813
AND ALL YOU CARE ABOUT
IS MONEY.

2169
01:30:51,847 --> 01:30:53,348
WELL, MAYBE YOU NEED
SOME TIME ALONE

2170
01:30:53,382 --> 01:30:55,283
TO THINK ABOUT
YOUR PRIORITIES.

2171
01:30:55,317 --> 01:30:58,120
[FRANK SQUEALS]

2172
01:30:58,153 --> 01:31:00,188
OH.

2173
01:31:01,557 --> 01:31:03,492
♪♪ [THEME]

2174
01:32:05,387 --> 01:32:07,055
WHAT'S GONNA
BECOME OF US NOW?
